`window.__hubCheck.pass === true` |\\n| **M9** | Workshop | the editor (section 5.21) + Dev \\\"Edit this level\\\" + export, import, slots | the editor suite passes (build, validate, save/load round trip, a test play won by script) |\\n| **M10** | Finish | the full scripted playthrough; the balance pass with dev sliders (update the defaults); the bug bash; final bundle; About pages and `exit-interview.json`; screenshot review | every check is green; no `TODO/FIXME/placeholder` anywhere; the bundle is the only file needed to play |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\\n\\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk / decision |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Japanese architecture in a height-map engine** (one column per cell, no passages under things) | walkable sloped roofs and enterable rooms with roofs are both impossible as geometry | decided: flat walkable roofs with drawn kawara caps (eaves, hips, ridge); halls are enterable but their roofs are visual (they fade when you're inside). Prototype in M1 with the kura and one hall, and check the sorting with the hero on a roof edge, behind a hall and inside a hall in all 8 camera turns |\\n| **Stealth fairness from a high iso camera** (the player sees more than the ninja) | trivializes stealth | Shadow Sight + Ki sensing (section 5.5); assist toggles; tuned with sliders; the perception tests pin the rules (lit vs dark, crouch, look-up, smoke) |\\n| **Grapple targeting** on pad, keys and mouse | frustration if it picks the wrong edge | a visible highlight at all times; hold-to-aim with slow motion; mouse picks under the cursor; tests list the anchors at fixed spots |\\n| **Paired-action animation quality** (10 cut choreographies, grapple, drag) | jerky or ugly kills ruin the signature moment | build on the engine's `takedown` structure and `E.move` poses; check every one with `filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`; keep them short (<1.3 s) |\\n| **Boss AI and telegraphs** | unfair or broken fights | each boss is a data-driven pattern script with red decals and long wind-ups; a bot fight test per boss (god mode + scripted attacks) asserts defeat in <90 s and that every move fires at least once |\\n| **Escort AI** | stuck followers break M2 | ground-only route through the opened water gate; a teleport-to-hero fallback when he is >160 away and out of the player's sight; an M2 escort test |\\n| **Swimming visuals** | the body would draw on top of the water | draw 10 units lower with a translucent water overlay queued above the waist; while diving, a dark silhouette and bubbles only; screenshot check |\\n| **AI Hub compliance** | a failed harness keeps the game out of the hub | build M8 against the real harness early (a spike in M4: a bare `hubCard` + trial greybox through the harness); follow section 5.22 to the letter; progress every second from 0; result on `time-up` |\\n| **Single-file bundling** (session.js first, inline 1.2 MB engine, `</script>` escapes, `file://`) | subtle load-order or escaping bugs | `build.mjs` asserts the head order and the escapes; a browser test opens the bundle from `file://` and checks the title scene and zero console errors |\\n| **Gibberish voice** | harsh, too loud, or spamming | profiles clamp the volume; a voice bus with its own setting; one dialog voice at a time; a 2 s bark cooldown; a browser listening check |\\n| **10-foot legibility and the HTML Shell** | default 13–14 px Shell text is tiny on a TV | patch #6 scales by window height; the canvas HUD scales with pixels; screenshot review at 1080p and 4K |\\n| **Attract mode getting stuck** | the demo loop must never freeze | 8 s beat timeouts; a 25 s vignette cap; cheats; a 3-loop headless test |\\n| **Workshop scope creep** | the editor can swallow time | a fixed feature list (section 5.21); built last (M9) on the existing loader and renderer; it is complete when its tests pass |\\n| **Determinism and flaky tests** | hub seeding and replays need stable gameplay | fixed-step engine; gameplay randomness only in update; cosmetic `crand` in draw; tests seed `Math.random = E.rng(7)`; a same-input → same-hash test |\\n| **Input conflicts** (the d-pad moves in menus but means tools in play; browser shortcuts) | broken controls | custom play movement without the d-pad (section 4.1); no Ctrl bindings; `preventDefault` on Tab and Space (the engine does it for bound keys; verify) |\\n| **Performance** (unlimited budget, but hitches are still bad UX) | first-time bakes per camera turn | bake floors and walls for the starting view in the level's boot step; accept a first-turn bake; shared FlowFields; canvas lighting tuned, GPU when available |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Testing (`tests/run.mjs` — one command, failures only, one-line count)\\n\\n### 9.1 The runner\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs [filter…]`:\\n  - runs `tools/build.mjs --js` first;\\n  - for each `tests/*.test.mjs` (filtered by name), creates a **fresh `node:vm` context** with stubs (`window`,\\n    `addEventListener`, `location`, an in-memory `localStorage`, `matchMedia` → false, `navigator`), loads\\n    `engine/my-3d2dge.js` + `build/game.js`, and seeds `Math.random = E.rng(7)`;\\n  - calls the test's default export with a helper `t`:\\n\\n    ```text\\n    t.game, t.E, t.B, t.I, t.snap(), t.step(sec), t.tap(a), t.hold(a, on), t.intent(obj, sec),\\n    t.load(missionId, { character, loadout, checkpoint }), t.check(name, cond, detail)\\n    ```\\n\\n  - then runs `tests/browser/*.mjs` (Playwright) unless `--fast`.\\n- It prints **only** `FAIL <suite> › <check>: <detail>` lines, then **one line**:\\n  `<passed>/<total> checks passed, <failed> failed (<seconds>s)`. Exit code 1 on any failure.\\n- Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (filter by suite name).\\n- Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit (TASK.md). Do run the tests and read the screenshots\\n  yourself.\\n- **`game.debug`** (also `window.__BENTOU.debug`), used by the tests and `tools/check.mjs`:\\n\\n  ```text\\n  snapshot() → { scene, mode, mission, t,\\n    hero{x,y,z,hp,state,crouch,swim,dive,breath,stamina,tool,stacks},\\n    guards[{id,type,x,y,z,state,level,alive,vis}], ki, light, exposure, detections, silentCuts, kills,\\n    civiliansHarmed, objectives{}, score, rank, boss{id,hp,phase}, escort{hp,state}, timer, flags,\\n    attract{vignette,beat}, hub{phase,sent,progress}, editor{} }\\n  teleport(x,y,z,f), cell(cx,cy), load(id,opts), go(scene,data), tune(k,v), resetTune(), cheat(name,on),\\n  give(tool,n), kill(id), alert(id|'all'), calm(), complete(objId), win(rank), fail(), autopilot(routeId), hash()\\n  ```\\n\\n### 9.2 Suites (each check uses fixed spots in test levels or the campaign maps)\\n\\n| Suite | Checks |\\n|---|---|\\n| `boot` | title after boot; attract after 10.5 s idle, and *not* before 10 s; any key, pad press or mouse move exits it; no errors |\\n| `input` | labels per device (keys \\\"Space\\\"; pad \\\"✕\\\" by default, \\\"A\\\" after the setting); prompts change with `lastDevice`; the d-pad doesn't move the hero in play but cycles tools; wheel taps cycle tools; the touch-only gate (stubs) shows the notice and hides the menu |\\n| `move` | run/walk/crouch speeds; vault 14; climb a 30 wall; can't climb 40 (needs the grapple); hop down; fall damage over 72; swim in `~`, dive unseen, breath runs out → damage; shallow water slows; wall hug engages, peek extends sight |\\n| `grapple` | the anchor is found at a kura edge; a tap pulls the hero onto the roof (z = 48); no anchor through a wall; range and rise limits follow the sliders; the mouse picks the nearer anchor |\\n| `perception` | a lit hero at 80 in the cone becomes alert in under 2 s; a crouched hero in shadow at 100 stays calm 5 s; a hero on a roof directly above is unseen; running at 50 is heard, crouching isn't; smoke blocks sight; grass hides; lightning exposes; a body is found → Heightened + bell run |\\n| `ki` | the Ki number is right at a known distance; Shadow Sight hides a guard behind a wall, senses it within range, hides it beyond; Focus extends it and reveals a disguised ninja |\\n| `alarm` | the bell rings after the runner arrives; the reinforcements spawn after the delay; killing the runner prevents the ring; music layers turn on and off |\\n| `silentcut` | every kind triggers from its geometry and not outside it (angles, heights, water); never on an alert guard or a boss; counters and score; `timeScale` restored to 1 afterwards; both characters' actions run to the end |\\n| `combat` | combos deal the listed damage; block reduction per character; a parry inside the window staggers, outside fails; riposte kills; the roll is invulnerable; i-frames; death → game over overlay; retry restores the checkpoint snapshot exactly |\\n| `tools` | each of the 10 tools does what section 5.9 says (one or more checks each); stacks and compartments; unlocks gate the shelf |\\n| `ai` | patrols follow routes and waits; post sweeps; sleepers wake on loud noise; eaters take baits; hounds smell and bark; archers shoot only with a clear line; ninja climb onto roofs; civilians scream and flee |\\n| `bosses` | each boss: intro, every move fires at least once, phase 2 triggers at its threshold, the bot wins in <90 s with god mode, the arena opens, defeat lines |\\n| `mission` | objective ordering (`after`), optional objectives, triggers fire once, timer fail (M3), escort fail (M2), the generic `mission.fail(reason)` hook, checkpoints; the score formula on a scripted run equals the hand-computed value; rank thresholds; unlocks; save round trip |\\n| `story` | every briefing and cutscene id exists and runs to completion when skipped; character-specific lines exist for both |\\n| `playthrough` | **the whole game, scripted**: New Story (Sojiro) → crawl → Trial → M1 → M2 → M3 → ending → credits → title, using the autopilot routes (cheats allowed: teleports, god mode); asserts each mission succeeded, results shown, unlocks granted, the save shows all completed, no errors. Then M1 as Kaede |\\n| `attract` | 3 loops, each vignette visited, no errors, beat timeouts never needed in a normal loop (log if they are) |\\n| `dev` | every toggle and action changes the state it names; each slider changes `B.T()` live; Reset page / Reset all restore the defaults |\\n| `workshop` | create a level via the editor API (paint walls, place hero, target, exit, guards with routes); validation catches a missing exit and an unreachable target; save/load and export/import round trips are identical; a test play is completed by the autopilot |\\n| `hub` (mock) | inject a fake `AIHub` before load (`active: true`; records calls; emits `card`/`start`/`message`/`leave`/`time-up`/`end`): `connect({mode:'ghost',seats:[1,4],card:true})`; `ready()` with no key; Enter → `answer('ready')`, △ → `answer('more')`; no `Math.random` calls on the card (spy); play starts at `time() >= 0`; `progress` every second from 0; `send` at about 10 Hz unreliable; ghosts drawn and removed on `leave`; `result` within 1 s of `time-up`; `end` stops input and sound; quit and dev mode unavailable |\\n| `determinism` | 30 s of scripted input in M1, twice → the same `hash()` |\\n| `browser/bundle` | opens the bundle from `file://` (Playwright Chromium): head order (meta charset, then the session script, then the hub metas), title scene, zero console errors, glyph switching on a fake gamepad, touch emulation (`hasTouch`, `isMobile`) shows the notice, attract after 10 s |\\n| `browser/hub` | copies the bundle + `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into `dev/.hubtest/`, starts `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (parses the port; checks the frame title is ours), runs `harness.html?game=<file>&players=2&auto=1`, then `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, then `&scenario=host-leave`; waits for `body[data-complete=true]`; asserts `window.__hubCheck.pass`; prints failing check names; kills the server **by its PID** |\\n\\n### 9.3 Engine tools\\n\\n- `node handoff/tools/check.mjs <bundle>#mission` (errors, fill, colors, look notes, snapshot) at every milestone.\\n- `filmstrip.mjs` for every attack, cut, grapple and boss move.\\n- `asset-sheet.mjs` for every new shape.\\n\\n### 9.4 Balance pass (M10)\\n\\n- Play each mission with both characters at Ninja difficulty. Tune with the dev sliders until:\\n  - a careful stealth run reaches Makunouchi;\\n  - a perfect run reaches Grand Kaiseki;\\n  - a loud run still finishes, at Hinomaru.\\n- Write the final values back into the TUNE defaults, and update the score-test expectations.\\n\\n### 9.5 Screenshots (only what scripts can't judge)\\n\\nReview each against the look target (Symphony of the Night / Legend of Mana grade, not NES):\\n\\n- the title;\\n- the Trial yard at dusk and at night;\\n- M1 rooftops with lanterns;\\n- the M1 feast hall (roof cap faded);\\n- the M2 lake in rain with lightning;\\n- the M3 keep and the moon;\\n- each boss mid-fight;\\n- the Silent Cut splash;\\n- the bento screen; results with the stamp;\\n- the HUD with PS, Xbox, keyboard and mouse prompts;\\n- the touch-only notice;\\n- the Workshop;\\n- the hub card with 4 names;\\n- the Shell menus at 1080p and 4K;\\n- the swim and dive views.\\n\\nCheck legibility at the size a TV shows.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 10. Final checklist (and what to write at the end)\\n\\n- [ ] `<root>/Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174734.html` plays from `file://` with no other file.\\n- [ ] Everything in section 0's scope works: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; every menu item does what it says.\\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs` passes, including the playthrough and the real hub harness.\\n- [ ] About pages hold the Source Information and the three feedback sets. The same text goes in your final chat\\n      reply.\\n- [ ] `<root>/exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape, every value filled (\\\"unknown\\\" where you can't confirm);\\n      check that it parses (`node -e \\\"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\\\"`).\\n      Pre-filled parts:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins\\\",\\n  \\\"tagline\\\": \\\"Seen by none. Fed by all.\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"An isometric ninja stealth-action game: pack your bento of tools, slip past lantern-lit guards, land Silent Cuts and earn your rank across a feudal night of missions, bosses and a mission editor.\\\",\\n  \\\"type\\\": \\\"Game\\\",\\n  \\\"genre\\\": \\\"Stealth\\\",\\n  \\\"source\\\": \\\"Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins\\\",\\n  \\\"series\\\": \\\"Tenchu\\\",\\n  \\\"players\\\": \\\"1–4\\\",\\n  \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Move WASD/left stick · Jump Space/✕ · Crouch C/○ · Strike click/□ · Grapple G/R1 · Tool R/R2 · Block right click/L1\\\",\\n  \\\"tags\\\": [\\\"pixel art\\\", \\\"isometric\\\", \\\"third-person\\\", \\\"story\\\", \\\"boss fights\\\", \\\"retro\\\"]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n- **Source Information values to carry over:**\\n  - Source: *Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins* (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000).\\n  - Plan: `PLAN.md`.\\n  - Genre: stealth-action (ninja assassination) with melee combat. Perspective: isometric third person, rotatable\\n    (engine `iso`; `threequarter` option).\\n  - Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (patched as listed), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, vanilla JS in one HTML\\n    file, Node + Playwright for tests.\\n  - Art direction: the engine's native PS1-era pixel art (320×240 expanded), HD Humanoid rigs, canvas + WebGPU\\n    lighting, procedural Japanese props and materials.\\n  - Animation: the engine's procedural rigs and `E.ACTIONS`, with new choreographies.\\n  - Audio: the engine's chip synth with Japanese-scale layered music + a WebAudio formant gibberish voice synth.\\n  - Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1–4 players.\\n  - Research: your own, plus the planner's (Wikipedia on Tenchu 2; the engine handoff docs; the AI Hub README and\\n    harness).\\n  - Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\\n  - Model and usage: yours.\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01Kd7czu1owFGjHZooqexnUb\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"9cdefc10-dd96-4250-9292-d55bd20762ae\",\"uuid\":\"96305884-dbd7-49f1-b0c2-6da7654914d2\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2060,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2060,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2650,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"a7b53f5c-978d-4f9d-bb68-62a0e9dca10d\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2800,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"c63a0448-cc13-4717-85de-1d4c123d952e\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"a98f53cf-f6e1-4a35-9bc2-6ab0c31c36d0\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3050,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"71b42c32-1d18-4a37-86e8-c12dc7c89677\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2070,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2070,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Kako114wVqhXXi2TKobWZA\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1026\\t- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.\\n1027\\t\\n1028\\tOn the first night Sonny hands you 20 free chips and explains the games. A prize counter swaps 300 chips for the\\n1029\\t\\\"Jackpot\\\" suit.\\n1030\\t\\n1031\\t**Fortuna Sevens (pachislot).**\\n1032\\t\\n1033\\t- 3 reels with 3 visible rows. Bet 1, 2 or 3 chips: 1 = the centre line, 2 = plus the top and bottom lines, 3 = plus\\n1034\\t  both diagonals.\\n1035\\t- ✕ / Space spins. Then ✕ ○ □ (J K L) stop reels 1, 2 and 3. A stop \\\"slips\\\" 0–4 symbols on the `casino` rng, so\\n1036\\t  timing matters a little.\\n1037\\t- Strips of 21 stops per reel. Payouts per line bet:\\n1038\\t\\n1039\\t| Line | Pays |\\n1040\\t| --- | --- |\\n1041\\t| 7-7-7 | ×100, with a jackpot fanfare and coin shower |\\n1042\\t| BAR-BAR-BAR | ×30 |\\n1043\\t| Sonny-Sonny-Sonny | ×20 (Sonny is wild) |\\n1044\\t| Volleyball ×3 | ×12 |\\n1045\\t| Palm ×3 | ×8 |\\n1046\\t| Coconut ×3 | ×5 |\\n1047\\t| Cherry, by count on the line | 1 ×2, 2 ×5, 3 ×10 |\\n1048\\t\\n1049\\t- Tune the strips so the RTP is **92% ± 3** at `T.slotsPayMul` 1 (a simulation test checks it).\\n1050\\t- Spinning reels show blur rows, then a stop clunk and a line highlight.\\n1051\\t\\n1052\\t**Blackjack.**\\n1053\\t\\n1054\\t- 6-deck shoe, reshuffled at 75%. The dealer stands on soft 17 (`T.dealerHitsSoft17` toggles it). Blackjack pays 3:2.\\n1055\\t  Double on any first two cards. Split once; split aces get one card each. No insurance, no surrender.\\n1056\\t- Bets of 1, 5, 10 or 25 chips (a stepper).\\n1057\\t- Controls: ✕/H hit, □/S stand, △/D double, R1/P split (only when legal), ○ leave between hands. Every button is also\\n1058\\t  clickable on screen.\\n1059\\t- Cards are pixel sprites (rank glyphs and suit sprites ♠ ♥ ♦ ♣ made with `E.sprite`), dealt with tweens and flipped.\\n1060\\t  Pepper has deadpan lines for a blackjack and a bust.\\n1061\\t\\n1062\\t**Roulette.**\\n1063\\t\\n1064\\t- A single-zero wheel in real order: 0, 32, 15, 19, 4, 21, 2, 25, 17, 34, 6, 27, 13, 36, 11, 30, 8, 23, 10, 5, 24, 16,\\n1065\\t  33, 1, 20, 14, 31, 9, 22, 18, 29, 7, 28, 12, 35, 3, 26.\\n1066\\t- **Betting layout:** a cursor moved with the stick, WASD or the mouse.\\n1067\\t\\n1068\\t| Bet | Pays |\\n1069\\t| --- | --- |\\n1070\\t| straight number | 35:1 |\\n1071\\t| red/black, odd/even, 1–18/19–36 | 1:1 |\\n1072\\t| dozens, columns | 2:1 |\\n1073\\t\\n1074\\t- Controls: ✕ place a chip (L1/R1 sizes 1/5/10/25), □ remove, △ spin, ○ leave.\\n1075\\t- An inset wheel shows the pocket ring turning while the ball spirals in, slows, bounces two pockets and settles. Then\\n1076\\t  the result is highlighted, payouts made, and a strip shows the last 10 results.\\n1077\\t- The dev-only toggle `T.rouletteDoubleZero` gives an American wheel.\\n1078\\t\\n1079\\tLeaving the casino ends the night and goes to the day-end card.\\n1080\\t\\n1081\\t### 4.17 Postcards (photo mode) and album (`42-photo.js`)\\n1082\\t\\n1083\\t**Where:** the pause menu's \\\"Take a Postcard\\\", or Create / C in walkable locations and on match results. Never in hub\\n1084\\tsessions or the attract. Gameplay time freezes (`timeScale` 0), while cosmetic motion (water, breathing idles) keeps\\n1085\\tgoing.\\n1086\\t\\n1087\\t**Controls:**\\n1088\\t\\n1089\\t| Input | Does |\\n1090\\t| --- | --- |\\n1091\\t| left stick / WASD | pan the focus |\\n1092\\t| right stick / right-drag | orbit at any angle (`game.rotateView`) |\\n1093\\t| L2/R2 / wheel | zoom .75–2.5 |\\n1094\\t| ✕ | take the photo |\\n1095\\t| ○ | exit |\\n1096\\t| □ | choose the subject: you, or any NPC present |\\n1097\\t| △ | the panel |\\n1098\\t| R3 / H | hide the UI |\\n1099\\t\\n1100\\tThe △ panel has:\\n1101\\t\\n1102\\t- **pose:** Wave, Peace, Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back, Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow;\\n1103\\t- **expression:** smile, shout, wince, neutral;\\n1104\\t- **filter:** Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow;\\n1105\\t- **frame:** none, or a postcard border with a \\\"Greetings from Isla Fortuna\\\" stamp and the date.\\n1106\\t\\n1107\\t**Taking a photo.** The shutter sound and a white flash, then a \\\"developing\\\" postcard slides to a corner. It is saved\\n1108\\tin `state.album` (at most 24; asks before replacing the oldest) as a **spec**, never pixels:\\n1109\\t`{ loc, day, slot, tod, weather, cam: { x, y, z, yaw, zoom, view }, people: [{ id, suit, acc, pose, expr, x, y, facing\\n1110\\t}], filter, frame }`.\\n1111\\t\\n1112\\t**The album** (Villa, or the menu for the latest save):\\n1113\\t\\n1114\\t- A 4×2 grid of live thumbnails: each spec is re-rendered at half size.\\n1115\\t- Opening one re-renders it full screen, live, so the palms still sway.\\n1116\\t- □ deletes (with a confirm); △ \\\"Set as title backdrop\\\"; R1 exports a PNG download (not in sessions).\\n1117\\t\\n1118\\tThe credits slideshow re-renders the album, plus a group photo taken automatically at the party.\\n1119\\t\\n1120\\t### 4.18 Story, dialogue, voices, cutscenes (`34-story.js`)\\n1121\\t\\n1122\\t- `E.Story` holds `people` for every speaker (portrait = their rig) and the nodes from `05-data-text.js`. Its `on`\\n1123\\t  events run game actions: `startMatch`, `giveMoney`, `giveItem`, `setPartner`, `openShop`, `photo`, `fade`.\\n1124\\t  `story.state()` goes in the save.\\n1125\\t- **The dialog box:** bottom, 2 lines, the name tag in the speaker's color, a portrait with expression\\n1126\\t  (`portraitOpts`), markup for emphasis (`{c=#ffd36a}…{/c}`, `{wave}`, `{shake}`). The Animalese voice runs from the\\n1127\\t  per-letter hook (patch 3). Text speed is a setting. Hold ○ or right click to fast-forward; Options on a cutscene asks\\n1128\\t  \\\"Skip scene?\\\".\\n1129\\t- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens, walk-ons (`game.tween` on bodies), emotes\\n1130\\t  (`story.emote(target, 'heart' | '!' | '?' | 'note' | 'dots')`), fades. The list is in §5.5.\\n1131\\t\\n1132\\t### 4.19 Save and load (`30-vacation.js`)\\n1133\\t\\n1134\\t**Slots:** `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave). The title's Load and the Villa journal's Save open `saves.show('load'\\n1135\\t| 'save')`. The game autosaves at every slot start; Continue loads `saves.latest()`.\\n1136\\t\\n1137\\t- `saves.write = () => ({ data: G.state, place: locationName, level: 'Day ' + day })`;\\n1138\\t- `read = save => G.loadState(save.data)`, with `version: 1` and a `migrate`.\\n1139\\t\\n1140\\t**State shape:**\\n1141\\t\\n1142\\t```js\\n1143\\t{ v: 1, seed, day: 1, slot: 0, weather: ['sunny', …], me: 'rin', money: 30000, chips: 0,\\n1144\\t  wardrobe: { suits: ['seigaiha'], acc: ['ribbon'] }, wearing: { suit: 'seigaiha', acc: ['ribbon'] },\\n1145\\t  npcWear: { lola: { suit: 'estrella', acc: ['sweatband'] }, … }, bag: { mango_smoothie: 1 },\\n1146\\t  affinity: { lola: 20, … }, mood: { lola: 'happy', … }, known: { lola: { hot_sauce: 'love' } },\\n1147\\t  partner: null, teams: [['lola', 'tess'], ['amara', 'mei']], record: { 'lola+tess': [0, 0] },\\n1148\\t  flags: {}, story: {}, chatted: {}, gifted: {}, album: [], titlePostcard: null,\\n1149\\t  stats: { matches: 0, wins: 0, points: 0, kills: 0, aces: 0, blocks: 0, poolBest: null, casinoNet: 0, gifts: 0,\\n1150\\t           photos: 0, earned: 0, spent: 0 } }\\n1151\\t```\\n1152\\t\\n1153\\t**New Vacation+** (after an ending) keeps the wardrobe, album and lifetime stats. It resets the days and affinity (to\\n1154\\tbase +10) and starts money at S$30,000 plus 10% of your final money.\\n1155\\t\\n1156\\t**Unlocks** for Beach Match (suits ever owned; everything after the first ending) live in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\\n1157\\t\\n1158\\t### 4.20 Front end: boot, title, menu, How to Play, About (`50-title.js`)\\n1159\\t\\n1160\\t**Boot.** Boot steps build the rigs, maps, music and caches behind the engine's boot screen, with messages: \\\"Raking the\\n1161\\tsand\\\", \\\"Inflating volleyballs\\\", \\\"Chilling the smoothies\\\", \\\"Counting Sonny's chips\\\", \\\"Polishing the golden sunglasses\\\".\\n1162\\t\\n1163\\t**Title.**\\n1164\\t\\n1165\\t- A sunset beach backdrop: sea layers, the sun, distant islands, palms, gentle waves.\\n1166\\t- The six fighters stand on the sand in their signature suits, each with her own idle: Rin stretching, Lola flexing,\\n1167\\t  Ingrid fanning herself, Amara dancing, Tess juggling a ball, Mei waving. Now and then Sonny jogs across the background\\n1168\\t  with a giant trophy.\\n1169\\t- The logo **AHEAD OR ALIVE**: `E.font.title` scale 4, colors `['#fff7d6', '#ffd36a', '#ff9e5e', '#ff5f7a']`, depth 3,\\n1170\\t  with a small spinning volleyball beside it. Under it **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL** at scale 2, white with a teal shadow.\\n1171\\t- A blinking \\\"PRESS ✕\\\" in the current device's glyph.\\n1172\\t- A footer with the version label (`E.versionLabel()`) and \\\"An original parody-tribute game\\\".\\n1173\\t- If a postcard is set as the title backdrop, it renders behind the logo instead.\\n1174\\t\\n1175\\t**Main menu.** A big list on the left; a turning fighter preview on the right.\\n1176\\t\\n1177\\t- **New Vacation**\\n1178\\t- **Continue** (if a save exists)\\n1179\\t- **Load**\\n1180\\t- **Beach Match**\\n1181\\t- **Album** (if there are postcards)\\n1182\\t- **How to Play**\\n1183\\t- **Settings** (`game.menu('settings')`)\\n1184\\t- **About & Credits**\\n1185\\t\\n1186\\t10 s idle starts the attract mode.\\n1187\\t\\n1188\\t**How to Play.** 10 pages, one idea each, with a live mini-scene in the panel and the current device's glyphs:\\n1189\\t\\n1190\\t1. Moving and the ring\\n1191\\t2. The touch chain: bump, set, spike\\n1192\\t3. Aiming and shots\\n1193\\t4. Serving\\n1194\\t5. Blocking and diving\\n1195\\t6. Calls and chemistry\\n1196\\t7. The vacation: slots, map, money\\n1197\\t8. Friends and gifts\\n1198\\t9. Casino and Pool Hop\\n1199\\t10. Postcards\\n1200\\t\\n1201\\t**About & Credits.** Pages turned with L1/R1, left/right or the on-screen arrows; the stick scrolls; large text, one\\n1202\\tfield per line. Contents in §10:\\n1203\\t\\n1204\\t1. Credits\\n1205\\t2. Source Information\\n1206\\t3. Testing Feedback\\n1207\\t4. Engine Feedback\\n1208\\t5. Prompt Feedback\\n1209\\t\\n1210\\t### 4.21 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\\n1211\\t\\n1212\\t**Trigger.** 10.0 s without input on `title` or `menu`. Input means any key, a pad button, a stick past its dead zone,\\n1213\\tthe mouse moving more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, or a touch; each resets the timer.\\n1214\\t\\n1215\\t**Playlist.** A director kept alive across scenes (`game.script(…, { keep: true })` plus the overlay watcher) plays it,\\n1216\\tre-seeded each cycle for variety. Demo scenes run on a throwaway demo state, never the player's save.\\n1217\\t\\n1218\\t1. **Match, about 50 s.** AI vs AI on Sunset Courts with random fighters, outfits and time of day: `spectacle` AI, the\\n1219\\t   camera cutting between Broadcast and Serve Cam every 2 points, commentary and highlight replays on.\\n1220\\t2. **Vacation montage, about 50 s.** 7 beats of 6–8 s, each with a big caption banner:\\n1221\\t\\n1222\\t| Caption | Shows |\\n1223\\t| --- | --- |\\n1224\\t| FIVE DAYS IN PARADISE | the island map flying from morning to night |\\n1225\\t| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"a610109c-7632-4563-8ba3-f09b06fff2ef\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:36:24.146Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.\\n\\nOn the first night Sonny hands you 20 free chips and explains the games. A prize counter swaps 300 chips for the\\n\\\"Jackpot\\\" suit.\\n\\n**Fortuna Sevens (pachislot).**\\n\\n- 3 reels with 3 visible rows. Bet 1, 2 or 3 chips: 1 = the centre line, 2 = plus the top and bottom lines, 3 = plus\\n  both diagonals.\\n- ✕ / Space spins. Then ✕ ○ □ (J K L) stop reels 1, 2 and 3. A stop \\\"slips\\\" 0–4 symbols on the `casino` rng, so\\n  timing matters a little.\\n- Strips of 21 stops per reel. Payouts per line bet:\\n\\n| Line | Pays |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| 7-7-7 | ×100, with a jackpot fanfare and coin shower |\\n| BAR-BAR-BAR | ×30 |\\n| Sonny-Sonny-Sonny | ×20 (Sonny is wild) |\\n| Volleyball ×3 | ×12 |\\n| Palm ×3 | ×8 |\\n| Coconut ×3 | ×5 |\\n| Cherry, by count on the line | 1 ×2, 2 ×5, 3 ×10 |\\n\\n- Tune the strips so the RTP is **92% ± 3** at `T.slotsPayMul` 1 (a simulation test checks it).\\n- Spinning reels show blur rows, then a stop clunk and a line highlight.\\n\\n**Blackjack.**\\n\\n- 6-deck shoe, reshuffled at 75%. The dealer stands on soft 17 (`T.dealerHitsSoft17` toggles it). Blackjack pays 3:2.\\n  Double on any first two cards. Split once; split aces get one card each. No insurance, no surrender.\\n- Bets of 1, 5, 10 or 25 chips (a stepper).\\n- Controls: ✕/H hit, □/S stand, △/D double, R1/P split (only when legal), ○ leave between hands. Every button is also\\n  clickable on screen.\\n- Cards are pixel sprites (rank glyphs and suit sprites ♠ ♥ ♦ ♣ made with `E.sprite`), dealt with tweens and flipped.\\n  Pepper has deadpan lines for a blackjack and a bust.\\n\\n**Roulette.**\\n\\n- A single-zero wheel in real order: 0, 32, 15, 19, 4, 21, 2, 25, 17, 34, 6, 27, 13, 36, 11, 30, 8, 23, 10, 5, 24, 16,\\n  33, 1, 20, 14, 31, 9, 22, 18, 29, 7, 28, 12, 35, 3, 26.\\n- **Betting layout:** a cursor moved with the stick, WASD or the mouse.\\n\\n| Bet | Pays |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| straight number | 35:1 |\\n| red/black, odd/even, 1–18/19–36 | 1:1 |\\n| dozens, columns | 2:1 |\\n\\n- Controls: ✕ place a chip (L1/R1 sizes 1/5/10/25), □ remove, △ spin, ○ leave.\\n- An inset wheel shows the pocket ring turning while the ball spirals in, slows, bounces two pockets and settles. Then\\n  the result is highlighted, payouts made, and a strip shows the last 10 results.\\n- The dev-only toggle `T.rouletteDoubleZero` gives an American wheel.\\n\\nLeaving the casino ends the night and goes to the day-end card.\\n\\n### 4.17 Postcards (photo mode) and album (`42-photo.js`)\\n\\n**Where:** the pause menu's \\\"Take a Postcard\\\", or Create / C in walkable locations and on match results. Never in hub\\nsessions or the attract. Gameplay time freezes (`timeScale` 0), while cosmetic motion (water, breathing idles) keeps\\ngoing.\\n\\n**Controls:**\\n\\n| Input | Does |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| left stick / WASD | pan the focus |\\n| right stick / right-drag | orbit at any angle (`game.rotateView`) |\\n| L2/R2 / wheel | zoom .75–2.5 |\\n| ✕ | take the photo |\\n| ○ | exit |\\n| □ | choose the subject: you, or any NPC present |\\n| △ | the panel |\\n| R3 / H | hide the UI |\\n\\nThe △ panel has:\\n\\n- **pose:** Wave, Peace, Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back, Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow;\\n- **expression:** smile, shout, wince, neutral;\\n- **filter:** Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow;\\n- **frame:** none, or a postcard border with a \\\"Greetings from Isla Fortuna\\\" stamp and the date.\\n\\n**Taking a photo.** The shutter sound and a white flash, then a \\\"developing\\\" postcard slides to a corner. It is saved\\nin `state.album` (at most 24; asks before replacing the oldest) as a **spec**, never pixels:\\n`{ loc, day, slot, tod, weather, cam: { x, y, z, yaw, zoom, view }, people: [{ id, suit, acc, pose, expr, x, y, facing\\n}], filter, frame }`.\\n\\n**The album** (Villa, or the menu for the latest save):\\n\\n- A 4×2 grid of live thumbnails: each spec is re-rendered at half size.\\n- Opening one re-renders it full screen, live, so the palms still sway.\\n- □ deletes (with a confirm); △ \\\"Set as title backdrop\\\"; R1 exports a PNG download (not in sessions).\\n\\nThe credits slideshow re-renders the album, plus a group photo taken automatically at the party.\\n\\n### 4.18 Story, dialogue, voices, cutscenes (`34-story.js`)\\n\\n- `E.Story` holds `people` for every speaker (portrait = their rig) and the nodes from `05-data-text.js`. Its `on`\\n  events run game actions: `startMatch`, `giveMoney`, `giveItem`, `setPartner`, `openShop`, `photo`, `fade`.\\n  `story.state()` goes in the save.\\n- **The dialog box:** bottom, 2 lines, the name tag in the speaker's color, a portrait with expression\\n  (`portraitOpts`), markup for emphasis (`{c=#ffd36a}…{/c}`, `{wave}`, `{shake}`). The Animalese voice runs from the\\n  per-letter hook (patch 3). Text speed is a setting. Hold ○ or right click to fast-forward; Options on a cutscene asks\\n  \\\"Skip scene?\\\".\\n- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens, walk-ons (`game.tween` on bodies), emotes\\n  (`story.emote(target, 'heart' | '!' | '?' | 'note' | 'dots')`), fades. The list is in §5.5.\\n\\n### 4.19 Save and load (`30-vacation.js`)\\n\\n**Slots:** `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave). The title's Load and the Villa journal's Save open `saves.show('load'\\n| 'save')`. The game autosaves at every slot start; Continue loads `saves.latest()`.\\n\\n- `saves.write = () => ({ data: G.state, place: locationName, level: 'Day ' + day })`;\\n- `read = save => G.loadState(save.data)`, with `version: 1` and a `migrate`.\\n\\n**State shape:**\\n\\n```js\\n{ v: 1, seed, day: 1, slot: 0, weather: ['sunny', …], me: 'rin', money: 30000, chips: 0,\\n  wardrobe: { suits: ['seigaiha'], acc: ['ribbon'] }, wearing: { suit: 'seigaiha', acc: ['ribbon'] },\\n  npcWear: { lola: { suit: 'estrella', acc: ['sweatband'] }, … }, bag: { mango_smoothie: 1 },\\n  affinity: { lola: 20, … }, mood: { lola: 'happy', … }, known: { lola: { hot_sauce: 'love' } },\\n  partner: null, teams: [['lola', 'tess'], ['amara', 'mei']], record: { 'lola+tess': [0, 0] },\\n  flags: {}, story: {}, chatted: {}, gifted: {}, album: [], titlePostcard: null,\\n  stats: { matches: 0, wins: 0, points: 0, kills: 0, aces: 0, blocks: 0, poolBest: null, casinoNet: 0, gifts: 0,\\n           photos: 0, earned: 0, spent: 0 } }\\n```\\n\\n**New Vacation+** (after an ending) keeps the wardrobe, album and lifetime stats. It resets the days and affinity (to\\nbase +10) and starts money at S$30,000 plus 10% of your final money.\\n\\n**Unlocks** for Beach Match (suits ever owned; everything after the first ending) live in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\\n\\n### 4.20 Front end: boot, title, menu, How to Play, About (`50-title.js`)\\n\\n**Boot.** Boot steps build the rigs, maps, music and caches behind the engine's boot screen, with messages: \\\"Raking the\\nsand\\\", \\\"Inflating volleyballs\\\", \\\"Chilling the smoothies\\\", \\\"Counting Sonny's chips\\\", \\\"Polishing the golden sunglasses\\\".\\n\\n**Title.**\\n\\n- A sunset beach backdrop: sea layers, the sun, distant islands, palms, gentle waves.\\n- The six fighters stand on the sand in their signature suits, each with her own idle: Rin stretching, Lola flexing,\\n  Ingrid fanning herself, Amara dancing, Tess juggling a ball, Mei waving. Now and then Sonny jogs across the background\\n  with a giant trophy.\\n- The logo **AHEAD OR ALIVE**: `E.font.title` scale 4, colors `['#fff7d6', '#ffd36a', '#ff9e5e', '#ff5f7a']`, depth 3,\\n  with a small spinning volleyball beside it. Under it **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL** at scale 2, white with a teal shadow.\\n- A blinking \\\"PRESS ✕\\\" in the current device's glyph.\\n- A footer with the version label (`E.versionLabel()`) and \\\"An original parody-tribute game\\\".\\n- If a postcard is set as the title backdrop, it renders behind the logo instead.\\n\\n**Main menu.** A big list on the left; a turning fighter preview on the right.\\n\\n- **New Vacation**\\n- **Continue** (if a save exists)\\n- **Load**\\n- **Beach Match**\\n- **Album** (if there are postcards)\\n- **How to Play**\\n- **Settings** (`game.menu('settings')`)\\n- **About & Credits**\\n\\n10 s idle starts the attract mode.\\n\\n**How to Play.** 10 pages, one idea each, with a live mini-scene in the panel and the current device's glyphs:\\n\\n1. Moving and the ring\\n2. The touch chain: bump, set, spike\\n3. Aiming and shots\\n4. Serving\\n5. Blocking and diving\\n6. Calls and chemistry\\n7. The vacation: slots, map, money\\n8. Friends and gifts\\n9. Casino and Pool Hop\\n10. Postcards\\n\\n**About & Credits.** Pages turned with L1/R1, left/right or the on-screen arrows; the stick scrolls; large text, one\\nfield per line. Contents in §10:\\n\\n1. Credits\\n2. Source Information\\n3. Testing Feedback\\n4. Engine Feedback\\n5. Prompt Feedback\\n\\n### 4.21 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\\n\\n**Trigger.** 10.0 s without input on `title` or `menu`. Input means any key, a pad button, a stick past its dead zone,\\nthe mouse moving more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, or a touch; each resets the timer.\\n\\n**Playlist.** A director kept alive across scenes (`game.script(…, { keep: true })` plus the overlay watcher) plays it,\\nre-seeded each cycle for variety. Demo scenes run on a throwaway demo state, never the player's save.\\n\\n1. **Match, about 50 s.** AI vs AI on Sunset Courts with random fighters, outfits and time of day: `spectacle` AI, the\\n   camera cutting between Broadcast and Serve Cam every 2 points, commentary and highlight replays on.\\n2. **Vacation montage, about 50 s.** 7 beats of 6–8 s, each with a big caption banner:\\n\\n| Caption | Shows |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| FIVE DAYS IN PARADISE | the island map flying from morning to night |\\n| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |\",\"numLines\":200,\"startLine\":1026,\"totalLines\":2180}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01Kako114wVqhXXi2TKobWZA\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"115a7101-8035-403c-a354-51f4f83a2992\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"714ed053-b5cc-45be-904d-add44ce0be82\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"99d4115e-ac85-4844-bf9c-39009e8f9714\",\"uuid\":\"6efa1551-6bae-4ce0-8bfa-cf6946434a04\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758__x42640e/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2097,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2097,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7100,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"2e6419b8-f0b8-4ae5-9e98-465cabee5c42\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7250,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"3c2ddb71-cd27-4fab-a35e-dc853d4b34c4\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"682a2a5b-f022-47de-896d-1725f856fafd\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":7550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"07d72fa0-3e0a-4abc-a856-6a3bd495de67\",\"uuid\":\"754337a7-52d5-4cb4-b4d7-4f0dcc525471\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":8,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183606__xf7f297/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174749__x8de669/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174758_