\"score\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"shots\\\\\\\":9}\\\\nkills 0 \\\\nscores\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01U1Mk8egiGRyzkGz7LJ6xyo\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"55c1395b-60b8-41b5-8bb2-51d8fac45cc1\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":250,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":200,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"e23968ce-5289-4f4d-ab20-7d83c63ef0c3\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":500,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":250,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"04ffb5bc-8b22-437d-90f2-1939afc1ee9a\\\"}\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184315__x1295cd/agent.out\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":157,\"oldLines\":3,\"newStart\":157,\"newLines\":4,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":1400,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":150,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"14f34045-19a9-4c91-b4b0-8ef52e3ad772\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"3fc75318-738f-4c07-bc4a-5f7d1d38e340\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":1600,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":200,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"14f34045-19a9-4c91-b4b0-8ef52e3ad772\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"6ae24faf-172d-4831-89fa-4a58accd7ea6\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":1850,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":250,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"14f34045-19a9-4c91-b4b0-8ef52e3ad772\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"034f8a57-71d5-4bb7-b932-6dc38fc8672b\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":2100,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":250,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"14f34045-19a9-4c91-b4b0-8ef52e3ad772\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"4cf5fe13-0b5d-4c1b-91ae-e48cf6896ab6\\\"}\"]}]},{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/agent.out\",\"hunks\":[{\"oldStart\":2363,\"oldLines\":3,\"newStart\":2363,\"newLines\":4,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":800,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":100,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"5f820ead-413b-4d29-ae10-f1836d6c35fa\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":900,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":100,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"2d8f7569-e80f-4073-a82e-62fc2355292b\\\"}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011Cgh3Smpx3XZMhdJQbHHdP\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"thinking\\\",\\\"thinking\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"signature\\\":\\\"\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":2257,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":589114,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":2257},\\\"output_tokens\\\":3,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"75b3de6c-1ca5-4a42-a236-bbecbff83136\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T01:46:04.051Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011Cgh3SmUcYRGF1pADsQmgU\\\",\\\"thinking_duration_ms\\\":17920,\\\"thinking_display\\\":\\\"updates\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011Cgh3Smpx3XZMhdJQbHHdP\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"PLAN.md is written, starting with the title. Nothing has been built yet; this stage only plans.\\\\n\\\\n**Title:** Snipeout HD (tagline *\\\\\\\"Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.\\\\\\\"*). I brainstormed 50 riffs on the name, none reusing \\\\\\\"Wipeout\\\\\\\", and Python's `secrets` picked #19. The deliverable will be `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174728.html`, with a dev folder of the same name.\\\\n\\\\n**What the plan specifies:**\\\\n- **Genre and camera:** an anti-gravity combat racer with a chase camera, plus a far chase, a cockpit view, look-back, and trackside TV cameras for intros, replays, spectating and the attract mode.\\\\n- **Tech:** the handoff engine runs everything, including scenes, input, menus, settings, the synthesized audio and the pixel-art HUD. The 3D picture comes from the same repo's 3D add-on, with three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 loaded from a CDN. All download URLs are pinned to the exact commits I researched, and the fetch commands were run once to confirm they work. The craft physics are custom and run without a browser, so headless tests and replays repeat exactly; the add-on's own kart physics can't handle these speeds or the tracks' tunnels, drops and overpasses.\\\\n- **Mechanics:** hover physics on banked tracks, analog airbrakes, pitch control, side-shift, barrel-roll boosts, speed pads and weapon pads, ten weapons, absorbing a weapon for shield, a pit strip, elimination and a launch boost.\\\\n- **Content:**\\\\n  - four tracks with full layouts and features;\\\\n  - six original teams with procedurally built craft, and 12 pilots;\\\\n  - four speed classes;\\\\n  - a 10-event season plus a 4-race Grand Prix, with written story beats;\\\\n  - an 11-drill tutorial;\\\\n  - six synthesized songs and gibberish-voiced announcer and dialogue.\\\\n- **Modes:** quick race, time trial with ghosts, hot lap, SNIPEOUT (combat points), OVERCLOCK (survive rising speed), replay, 2-player split screen, and AI Hub ghost races.\\\\n- **TASK.md's other requirements:** dev mode with about 35 live sliders and a reset, the 10-second attract mode, PlayStation button prompts by default with an Xbox option in Settings, and the touch-only notice. A checklist maps every requirement to where it lives and which test proves it.\\\\n- **Order:** 13 milestones, starting with a proof that the single-file 3D page loads at all. A full race with AI and weapons comes by the sixth.\\\\n- **Risks:** 13 are listed, each with how to de-risk it.\\\\n- **Testing:** one command that prints only failures and a count. It covers headless suites, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, browser checks, and the real AI Hub harness at 2 and 4 players, with network faults and the host leaving.\\\\n\\\\n**Checked during planning:**\\\\n- **Track layouts:** a script confirmed lengths of 3.8–5.0 km and tightest turns of 44–56 m. The two overpasses clear by 24.5 m and 31.9 m. Every jump flies at each class's speed; the Karakum gorge needs 75 m/s.\\\\n- **Handling model:** a quick simulation caught a flaw in my first draft. Lateral grip had no cap, so airbrakes didn't matter. The model is fixed, and its feel targets are now numbers the simulation reaches.\\\\n- **Lap times:** SPARK laps should run 46–59 s and SINGULARITY 27–34 s, so a 3-lap race takes about 1.5–3 minutes.\\\\n\\\\n**One thing about your machine:** `/tmp` is a shared tmpfs that sat at 97–99% full while I worked, and it briefly filled completely. The plan routes all temp files into the dev folder. My research copies and scripts are in `~/.cache/opus55-plan-x978410`.\\\"}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":2257,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":589114,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":2257},\\\"output_tokens\\\":3,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"0af7cd7c-7b61-489d-86ab-010715e3fe6f\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"7d53727a-4443-41bd-92ca-08defb3c904c\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T01:46:09.592Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011Cgh3SmUcYRGF1pADsQmgU\\\"}\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":0,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184315__x1295cd/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174728__x978410/agent.out\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01FRUihcDwRKhKUn8fh7GXTN\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"1ef49dbf-5b47-453e-a10f-aaca8fef2132\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":200,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":150,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"eb03b278-9d31-4e06-8b85-24d44a68ab66\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":300,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"3c819b0f-1b18-471b-b765-9dcf56869a17\",\"uuid\":\"1bfd8722-547d-4a51-a7f8-0789faaa6b8d\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2559,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2559,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":48,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":1,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"0dfd5435-afc3-43ce-beb9-f51b8af69793\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":209,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":161,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"2618bc8d-e229-4488-93db-207ce9547e22\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh3TAo4ZpFsQTnZsoy6v\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Tables are tidy now, and I'm adding a consolidated Settings list (§5.13) and an items, collectibles and unlockables note (§6.7), since TASK.md names those content types.\\n\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":729,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":583671,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":729},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"4891c383-7596-4629-b7a0-8efc841ea030\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:46:06.363Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh3TAUUC35X38dvNCVzy\",\"narration_block_indexes\":[0],\"thinking_duration_ms\":1,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}","+{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh3TAo4ZpFsQTnZsoy6v\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01DLgVZ8LLBghjUx74koTFon\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\np = 'PLAN.md'\\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\\nanchor = \\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 6. Content\\\\n\\\"\\nassert s.count(anchor) == 1\\nsettings = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\\n\\nThe engine's standard Settings and Controls screens are used as they are (no settings UI of our own): Display (full\\nscreen, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate), Sound (volume, music, effects, audio offset), Comfort (reduce\\nmotion, shake, flashes), Controls (rebinding per device, dead zone, vibration), plus `E.World3D.SETTINGS` (3D picture\\nPixels/Balanced/Full, shadows, filter; \\\"Characters\\\" cards/puppets for the crowd and hosts). Ours, via\\n`menu.settings` (group **Game**): **Button symbols** PlayStation / Xbox (E5), **Speed units** km/h / mph, **Default\\ncamera** Far / Close / Hood, **My ghost** on / off, **Coco's ghost** off / on, **Loop assist** on / off, **Steering\\nsensitivity** 0.5–1.5 (slider), **Hints** on / off (first-time tips). Subtitles are always on (voices are gibberish).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ns = s.replace(anchor, \\\"\\\\n\\\" + settings + anchor)\\nanchor2 = \\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 7. Art direction and animation\\\\n\\\"\\nassert s.count(anchor2) == 1\\nitems = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n### 6.7 Items, rivals and unlockables (what the player collects and fights)\\n\\nTrackMania has no pickups, and neither does CRACKMANIA: speed comes from the road. **On the track:** boost pads\\n(chevrons), checkpoints, kickers, loops, banked bends, dirt/ice/bumps surfaces. **Opponents:** the clock (medal\\ntimes), your own ghost, Coco's ghost (author time), the Ghost Guild in Survival, other players' ghosts in hot seat,\\nsplit screen and AI Hub rounds. **Collected and spent:** coppers (¢) from medals and Survival; medals (B/S/G/A) per\\ntrack and puzzle; Survival ranks; editor packs (STUNTS, LOOPS & BANKS, SURFACES, SCENERY); garage patterns; the three\\nenvironments and their cars; saved replays and custom tracks.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ns = s.replace(anchor2, \\\"\\\\n\\\" + items + anchor2)\\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint('ok')\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"^## \\\\|^### \\\" PLAN.md | head -80\",\"description\":\"Add Settings and Items sections and list the outline\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":729,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":583671,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":729},\"output_tokens\":4,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\",\"uuid\":\"c6fdb79a-2c4e-4463-9144-b4f6ffe5203a\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:46:14.032Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh3TAUUC35X38dvNCVzy\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01DLgVZ8LLBghjUx74koTFon\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np = 'PLAN.md'\\ns = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()\\nanchor = \\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 6. Content\\\\n\\\"\\nassert s.count(anchor) == 1\\nsettings = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\\n\\nThe engine's standard Settings and Controls screens are used as they are (no settings UI of our own): Display (full\\nscreen, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate), Sound (volume, music, effects, audio offset), Comfort (reduce\\nmotion, shake, flashes), Controls (rebinding per device, dead zone, vibration), plus `E.World3D.SETTINGS` (3D picture\\nPixels/Balanced/Full, shadows, filter; \\\"Characters\\\" cards/puppets for the crowd and hosts). Ours, via\\n`menu.settings` (group **Game**): **Button symbols** PlayStation / Xbox (E5), **Speed units** km/h / mph, **Default\\ncamera** Far / Close / Hood, **My ghost** on / off, **Coco's ghost** off / on, **Loop assist** on / off, **Steering\\nsensitivity** 0.5–1.5 (slider), **Hints** on / off (first-time tips). Subtitles are always on (voices are gibberish).\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ns = s.replace(anchor, \\\"\\\\n\\\" + settings + anchor)\\nanchor2 = \\\"\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## 7. Art direction and animation\\\\n\\\"\\nassert s.count(anchor2) == 1\\nitems = \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n### 6.7 Items, rivals and unlockables (what the player collects and fights)\\n\\nTrackMania has no pickups, and neither does CRACKMANIA: speed comes from the road. **On the track:** boost pads\\n(chevrons), checkpoints, kickers, loops, banked bends, dirt/ice/bumps surfaces. **Opponents:** the clock (medal\\ntimes), your own ghost, Coco's ghost (author time), the Ghost Guild in Survival, other players' ghosts in hot seat,\\nsplit screen and AI Hub rounds. **Collected and spent:** coppers (¢) from medals and Survival; medals (B/S/G/A) per\\ntrack and puzzle; Survival ranks; editor packs (STUNTS, LOOPS & BANKS, SURFACES, SCENERY); garage patterns; the three\\nenvironments and their cars; saved replays and custom tracks.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\ns = s.replace(anchor2, \\\"\\\\n\\\" + items + anchor2)\\nopen(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s)\\nprint('ok')\\nEOF\\ngrep -n \\\"^## \\\\|^### \\\" PLAN.md | head -80\",\"description\":\"Add Settings and Items sections and list the outline\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01DLgVZ8LLBghjUx74koTFon\":{\"cwd\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work\"}}}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01DLgVZ8LLBghjUx74koTFon\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"ok\\n15:## 0. Deliverables, names and ground rules\\n40:## 1. The game in one page\\n90:## 2. Technology and architecture\\n92:### 2.1 Stack (decided)\\n114:### 2.2 Getting the engine files\\n133:### 2.3 Units, axes and conventions (everyone must use these)\\n153:### 2.4 Engine changes (make them first, list them in `engine/CHANGES.md`, mention them in Engine Feedback)\\n166:### 2.5 Folder layout and modules\\n241:### 2.6 Runtime structure\\n272:### 2.7 Build to a single file\\n299:## 3. Player experience and controls\\n301:### 3.1 The core loop (must feel instant)\\n312:### 3.2 Input maps (`game.input` presets; prompts always from `game.input.label(action)` + our glyph sprites)\\n340:### 3.3 10-foot UI rules (apply everywhere)\\n358:## 4. Core systems\\n360:### 4.1 Blocks (the catalogue)\\n402:### 4.2 Block paths (centrelines and frames)\\n431:### 4.3 Geometry, materials and colliders\\n471:### 4.4 The car (validated model — build exactly this, then tune with Dev Mode)\\n587:### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\\n606:### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\\n621:### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\\n632:### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\\n655:### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\\n668:## 5. Modes and features\\n670:### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\\n702:### 5.2 Race (campaign)\\n719:### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\\n729:### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\\n766:### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\\n777:### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\\n792:### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\\n836:### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\\n844:### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\\n854:### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \\\"Dev Mode\\\")\\n873:### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\\n888:### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\\n904:### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\\n916:## 6. Content\\n918:### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\\n944:### 6.2 Environments\\n960:### 6.3 Race tracks (15) — programs validated on the 32×32 grid\\n996:### 6.4 Puzzles (6) — fixed blocks and inventories computed from validated solutions\\n1014:### 6.5 Survival gauntlets\\n1018:### 6.6 Scenery and trackside dressing (`track/deco.js`, seeded by track id)\\n1035:### 6.7 Items, rivals and unlockables (what the player collects and fights)\\n1046:## 7. Art direction and animation\\n1048:### 7.1 The look\\n1058:### 7.2 Textures (`env/textures.js`; bake with `E.mkCanvas(w, h)` → `THREE.CanvasTexture`, NearestFilter, repeat)\\n1067:### 7.3 Cars (`car/draw.js`, the pen, frame from E1; 25–45 parts each, outlines automatic)\\n1082:### 7.4 Characters and props\\n1109:### 7.5 Effects (game.particles in 3D, the pen, the camera)\\n1118:### 7.6 UI art (pixel sprites via `E.sprite`, `E.font`, `E.ui`)\\n1128:### 7.7 Animation list (everything that moves, built on the engine's rigs, tweens and scripts)\\n1140:## 8. Audio, story and text\\n1142:### 8.1 Music and sound (all synthesized; `game.audio` + `game.audio.ctx`)\\n1173:### 8.2 Story beats and characters (`story/story.js`)\\n1201:### 8.3 Writing style (TrackMania 2003's)\\n1211:### 8.4 Gibberish voices (`audio/babble.js`)\\n1224:## 9. Testing\\n1226:### 9.1 Headless loader (validated while planning: three r182 and Rapier load and step in Node 24)\\n1253:### 9.2 The one command\\n1266:### 9.3 Suites and what they check\\n1286:### 9.4 Rules for testing\\n1292:### 9.5 Browser checks (`tools/browser.mjs`, Playwright 1.63 + Chromium; built HTML opened from `file://`)\\n1306:### 9.6 AI Hub harness (`tools/hub.mjs`)\\n1318:## 10. Build order and milestones\\n1340:## 11. Risks and how to de-risk them\\n1359:## 12. Finishing: deliverables, About, exit interview, final 