{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user ran `/goal`: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A Stop hook blocks until satisfied.\n   - STAGE.md: \"Read TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how to build it, written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort) in this folder. Build the game TASK.md describes, following the plan and using the title it gives; where they disagree, TASK.md wins. Deliver everything TASK.md asks for, including its file name, and the sections it asks for in your final reply.\"\n   - TASK.md (source Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins): single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331].html in root; dev subfolder of same name; build on my-3d2dge dist/handoff (may change engine); all audio in code, Animalese/Simlish gibberish voices; AI Hub multiplayer per ai-hub lib/hub plus game standalone; feature-complete demo/vertical slice; dev mode from pause menu with live sliders + reset to defaults; attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menu (AI may cheat), any input exits; narrative tone like source; 10-foot controller-first UX (DualSense standard mapping, PS glyphs default with Settings option for Xbox A B X Y; keyboard/mouse native; hover moves focus; prompts follow last input; no dense web-style screens); touch-only: no touch controls, show \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract runs; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; Source Information/Testing Feedback/Engine Feedback/Prompt Feedback in chat reply AND in-game About/Credits screen (\"unknown\" if can't confirm); exit-interview.json in exact given shape.\n   - Constraints stated verbatim in TASK.md (must keep): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Also: \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" Plan: /tmp is a small, nearly full tmpfs — keep temp files inside the dev folder.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 engine (E = My3D2dge): E.Game (headless in Node, fixed step 1/120, game.advance), scenes, E.TileMap heights (one column per cell), E.Mover parkour/actions (E.ACTIONS paired actions like takedown), E.sees/E.hears/E.Suspicion (no decay while seen), E.FlowField, E.Humanoid rigs (rig.solvePose wrapping for joint post-processing, E.ik3), E.Shell HTML menus/settings, E.Dialog, E.Menu, game.settings groups, game.saves, audio step sequencer with layers, r.queue depth sort with footprint lift (sorts over actors on block), r.overlay draws on top (backgrounds must go to r.ctx), canvas lighting + optional WebGPU.\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0 (session.js unmodified, first script in head), ghost mode, own card, AIHub.connect/ready/answer/time/progress/result/send/on events, harness conformance (window.__hubCheck.pass).\n   - Game architecture: one IIFE from concatenated src files; B namespace with registries B.def/B.get, event bus B.on/B.emit; intent-driven hero (player, autopilot, tests); node:vm headless tests; Playwright browser tests.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (root = .../work; dev = root/Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331):\n   - root/Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331.html — final bundle (~1.74 MB), built by `node tools/build.mjs`.\n   - root/exit-interview.json — generated by `node tools/interview.mjs` from B.ABOUT; parses, no empty fields; aiHub: name \"Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins\", tagline \"Seen by none. Fed by all.\", type Game, genre Stealth, series Tenchu, players \"1–4\", tags ['pixel art','isometric','third-person','story','boss fights','retro'].\n   - dev/engine/my-3d2dge.js — patched copy (marked // BENTOU PATCH n): 1 font glyphs (✕○□△◀▶ · ° — … ’ ‘ ∞ ✓ ✗ in G57); 2 glyphs setting default 'playstation', options PlayStation/Xbox; 3 Humanoid gear (mask cloth/oni, hats jingasa/kabuto with crest, weapons spear/bow/club, offhand blade, sashimono); 4 Shell `s.rows` custom rows + Dev group excluded from Settings; 5 pointermove hover focuses; 6 --ui 10-foot scale (Normal=1, Auto/Large/Huge by innerHeight/720, zoom on panels, base font 16px, buttons min 52px, `.esh-mod` max-height:100%); 7 music track pluck/ring/attack/release; 8 audio.voiceBus + voiceVolume; 9 ignore pause while AIHub active and Pad8 held.\n   - dev/engine/PATCHES.md — lists the 9 patches. dev/index.html — dev page loading session.js, engine, build/game.js.\n   - dev/vendor/aihub/{session.js, harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md, examples}; dev/handoff/ (docs, tools, kits, node_modules playwright 1.63).\n   - dev/tools/build.mjs — ORDER: 00-core, 01-tune, 02-input, 03-glyphs, 05-game, 04-camera, 10-audio, 11-voice, 20-assets, 21-rigs, 30-world, 31-actors, 40-hero, 41-silentcut, 42-grapple, 43-combat, 44-tools, 50-perception, 51-guard-brain, 52-enemies, 53-bosses, 54-escort, 60-mission, 61-score, 62-story, 63-cutscene, 64-levels-training, 64-levels-m1, 64-levels-m2, 64-levels-m3, 64-levels-delivery, 65-missions, 70-hud, 71-scenes-menu, 72-scenes-story, 73-scene-mission, 74-dev, 75-workshop, 80-autopilot, 81-attract, 82-hub, 90-main; wraps in `(() => {\\n'use strict';\\nconst E = My3D2dge, { px, clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\\n ... })();`; fails on missing/unlisted files and /\\bTODO\\b|\\bFIXME\\b|placeholder|lorem/i; `--js` writes build/game.js only; full build writes root html with session.js first, hub metas (goal \"Silent kills, unseen, fast: top ninja score wins\", howto \"Move WASD/stick · Strike click/□ · Jump Space/✕ · Crouch C/○ · Tool R/R2\"), bootSplash('BENTOU 2'), escapes `</script`.\n   - dev/tests/run.mjs — THE test command `node tests/run.mjs [filter...] [--fast] [--browser]`; build({ jsOnly: fast }); fresh vm context per suite with stubs and seeded Math.random; helper t {game,E,B,I,snap,step,tap,hold,intent(obj,s) via B.testIntent,load,check,makeContext}; then browser suites; prints only FAIL lines + \"N/M checks passed, F failed (s)\".\n   - Tests: lib.mjs (yard level 30×24), routes.mjs (ROUTES + runRoute), suites boot, move, grapple, perception, ki, silentcut, combat, tools, ai, alarm, bosses (forced moves via Bosses.force, bot fight style 'plain' <90 s), mission (ordering, optional, timer fail → m3_fail cutscene → overlay, escort fail, fail hook, checkpoint restore, score formula, rank thresholds incl. 600 Hinomaru, detection cap, unlocks, save round trip), story (scenes exist/skip, char-specific lines, spoken lines exist, bark categories, poses tap/toast/bow), attract (3 loops, no timeouts), dev, workshop, input, determinism, hub (mock AIHub via `export const context = { hub: fake }`, vm.runInContext('Math', ctx) spy), playthrough (whole story + Kaede M1 + delivery), about (6 pages, interview consistency); browser/bundle.mjs (head order, title, fake DualSense glyph switching, attract at 10 s, mouse exits, #m1 after about:blank, touch-only notice on 390x844 hasTouch, no errors), browser/hub.mjs (copies bundle as .hubtest/game.html + harness files, spawns python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1, parses port, verifies title /Bentou 2/, runs players=2&auto=1, players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1, players=2&scenario=host-leave&auto=1, srv.kill()).\n   - dev/tools/shot.mjs, moments.mjs (named moment screenshots), hubshot.mjs, interview.mjs (writes exit-interview.json; `--print` prints markdown sections; splits Genre/perspective at first '; ').\n   - Key src details:\n     - 00-core: B, def/get/all/ids, bus, rand vs crand, helpers; `window.__BENTOU = B`.\n     - 01-tune: TUNE 32 sliders (darkness default changed to .8), DIFF multipliers, B.T(key), GAME_SETTINGS (uiScale, difficulty, camAngle, invertTurn, crouchHold, cones, marker, showAll, heartbeat, textSpeed, blood, voices), DEV_SETTINGS group 'Dev'.\n     - 02-input: B.INPUT action map (custom incl. menu actions), CONTROL_NAMES, any-input clock B.noteInput/B.lastInput, B.wheel, B.touchOnly(), B.mouseMode(), B.intentFromInput() (d-pad excluded from movement).\n     - 05-game: `new E.Game({... input: B.INPUT, menu: { items: () => B.pauseItems(), settings, controls, quit: HUBACTIVE ? false : 'title' }, camera: { zoom: false }, corner: !HUBACTIVE })`; ui = new E.Shell with theme.\n     - 30-world: World class (map + nav with deep water blocked, light map bake with map.ray LOS, dynStep per-step lights, blocks/caps with `ring` for tiers and occupied roofs, halls with fading roofs, bigMoon sky for M3 with outside false, flow cache LRU, steer, reachable, setCells).\n     - 41-silentcut: kinds back/side/front/above/undertow (undertow d<=24), cutSpec choreographies per character, presentation (slowmo, cine zoom, letterbox, splash).\n     - 43-combat: B.damage (boss strike damage ×.45 except riposte/fire/plunge; caged escort immune), enemyStrike parry window.\n     - 44-tools: 10 tools; smoke clouds blind guards (cough, cap mind .64); Tools.cd reset in MS.enter.\n     - 50-perception: SEE_MIN=.18; look-up gate uses target chest (t.z+22); B.noise(x,y,z,loud,kind,src) skips src.\n     - 51-guard-brain: guards ignore caged escort; snore/bark/shout noises pass src; freezeAI zeroes velocity.\n     - 53-bosses: four bosses, Bosses.force(b,name,M), b.moveLog, defeat lines in b.said.\n     - 60-mission: Mission.interact prefers interacts over escort toggle; `M.timerFail = true` on timer expiry.\n     - 61-score: RANKS [[2600,GK],[2000,M],[1400,E],[600,H],[-1e9,L]]; detections penalty -150*min(3,n).\n     - 62-story: prologue has ['pose','granny','tap']; m3_fail has ['pose','takanori','toast'] + caption; ending has toast pose.\n     - 63-cutscene: paintRoom(r, kind, over, flK=.78) draws to r.ctx; story scene uses flK .66, focus `(game.H/2 - game.H*.34)/-game.view.bz`; poses bow/tap/toast with poseT; sake cup drawn for toast.\n     - 21-rigs: Rigs.paddleTap(t), Rigs.toast(k) added.\n     - 73-scene-mission: MS.step (heartbeat sfx, fireflies, mouse-held interaction, timer cutscene: `if (M.result === 'fail' && M.timerFail && !M.timerCut ...) { M.timerCut = true; Cutscene.play('m3_fail', M.char, () => game.go('mission', { M }, { fade: 'dissolve' })); return; }`), game over overlay \"YOUR BOX IS EMPTY\", B.pauseItems.\n     - 70-hud: focus desaturation tint, d-pad hints at by+19, splash kanji spacing 33*s.\n     - 71-scenes-menu: MENU_SCENE/paper moved here (paper draws to r.ctx); title menu at left, heroes right, versionLine 'my-3D2dge v'+E.version+' - Bentou 2 v'+B.version; char select wide card under heading + greeting subtitle.\n     - 80-autopilot: beats incl. {interact: s}, fight with style 'plain', timeout `b.max || (b.fight ? b.fight + 1 : b.wait ? b.wait + 1 : 8)`, swim-aware fighting.\n     - 82-hub: hub card names stacked list,