{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghBYumnSSFDXnqAn8p4Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished the game, and the full test command passes: **320 of 320 checks** (`node tests/run.mjs`, 121 s). That includes a real run of the AI Hub harness and browser checks of the bundled file opened from file://.\n\n**Deliverables (in this folder's root)**\n- `Bentou2-Tenchu2-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331.html` is the single file, about 1.74 MB with everything inlined. It follows TASK.md's `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331]` pattern: GameTitle is `Bentou2` (from the plan's title, *Bentou 2: Birth of the Lunchbox Assassins*) and SOURCE is `Tenchu2`. The dev subfolder has the same name.\n- `exit-interview.json` parses, has every field filled in and matches TASK.md's shape.\n\n**Checking TASK.md item by item.** A new suite, `tests/task.test.mjs`, has one check for each TASK.md requirement, run against the built game. It passed 33 of 33:\n1. **Package:** the file name pattern, the file in the root, the dev folder with the same name, and nothing loaded from outside the file.\n2. **Title:** shown on the page and on the title screen.\n3. **Engine:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2, with all 9 changes marked `BENTOU PATCH`.\n4. **Art and animation:** new Japanese props and icons; ten Silent Cut takedowns, the grapple, and poses (paddle tap, toast, bow, and others).\n5. **Audio:** no audio or image files at all. Music, sound effects and the gibberish voices are generated in code.\n6. **Scope:** a training mission, three story missions each with a boss, and the Night Delivery. Two playable characters, 10 tools, 5 guard types, civilians and disguised enemies, and a mission editor.\n7. **Dev mode:** opens from the pause menu and has over 30 live sliders with reset to defaults.\n8. **Attract mode:** starts after 10 s idle on the title, the AI plays with god mode on, and any input exits it.\n9. **Multiplayer:** the AI Hub tags, with the session script first in `<head>`. The game also works on its own: the Shadow Trial races your best ghost.\n10. **Story tone:** opening crawl, briefings, more than 12 cutscenes, and more than 14 kinds of guard chatter.\n11. **Controls and prompts:**\n    - PlayStation button icons by default, with an Xbox option in Settings.\n    - The keyboard keys PC players expect, plus mouse aiming and clicks.\n    - The standard controller layout.\n    - On-screen prompts follow whichever input you used last.\n    - Hovering moves the focus.\n    - No dense screens.\n12. **Touch-only devices:** \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button, and attract mode still runs.\n13. **About / Credits screen and exit interview:** the in-game screen shows all four sections, and the JSON is in the right shape.\n14. **No leftovers:** no TODO, FIXME, placeholder or stub in the source.\n\nThe deeper behaviour behind each item is covered by the other suites: boot, dev, attract, hub, input, playthrough, about, and the two browser suites.\n\n**The issue count.** `tests/ISSUES.md` now lists every issue testing found, with how it was found and how it was fixed. There are 26: 17 caught by scripted tests (#1–17) and 9 by reviewing screenshots (#18–26). Four were critical (#6, #7, #12, #20). The in-game Testing Feedback now points to that file.\n\n## Source Information\n\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:33:31\n- **Source:** Tenchu 2: Birth of the Stealth Assassins (Acquire / Activision, PlayStation, 2000)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and perspective:** Third-person ninja stealth-action with melee combat and boss duels; isometric third person, rotatable in 45-degree steps and zoomable (engine iso view; three-quarter as a Settings option)\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (handoff package, patched: 9 changes listed in the credits), AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client 1.4.0 (unmodified), vanilla JavaScript in one HTML file; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 (Chromium) for the tests\n- **Art direction:** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art (320 x 240 expanded), HD Humanoid rigs dressed for the period, canvas lighting (WebGPU lighting where available), procedural Japanese props, materials, roof caps and wall painters\n- **Animation:** The engine's procedural rigs, E.MOVES and E.ACTIONS, with new paired choreographies (ten Silent Cuts, the grapple, the drag) and joint post-processing poses (the ninja run, the wall hug, eating, sleeping, swimming, the bow)\n- **Audio:** Music on the engine's step sequencer in Japanese scales (Hirajoshi, In) with koto, shamisen, shakuhachi, fue, drone and taiko voices and layered mission songs; synthesized sound effects; Animalese-style gibberish voices from a WebAudio formant synth\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1-4 players (Night Delivery); the Shadow Trial races your own best ghost on its own\n- **Testing:** One command (node tests/run.mjs: failures only and a one-line count, 320 checks): 22 suites in fresh node:vm pages driven by game.advance and game.debug, among them a TASK.md suite with one check a requirement, a scripted playthrough of the whole story, three attract loops and a mock hub; Playwright checks of the single file from file://; the real AI Hub harness (2 players; 4 with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5; the host leaving); screenshots only for the look\n- **Research:** The planner's research (the Wikipedia article on Tenchu 2; the engine's handoff docs; the AI Hub README and harness) plus the engine and hub docs read for this build; no web search during the build\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n- **Usage:** API cost and tokens: unknown (not visible to the agent). Session time: about 2 hours (18:33 to about 20:35).\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n**How many issues did testing catch?**\n26. The scripted tests caught 17 (in the game, the autopilot and the level data) and screenshot reviews caught 9 visual and layout issues. Each is listed in tests/ISSUES.md with how it was found and fixed.\n\n**How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?**\n4: guards attacking Tobei while he was still caged (the alarm bell could fail Kiri Lake), the water-gate lever taken by Tobei's wait / follow toggle (it blocked the escort), sleeping guards woken by their own snores (it broke the Sleep Dango and a Trial step), and the roof caps drawing over people standing on a roof (Kurogane's fight on the keep top was hidden).\n\n**What was the most helpful test you ran?**\nThe scripted playthrough of the whole story (autopilot routes through all four missions, the ending, the credits, Kaede's run and the Night Delivery). It found both Tobei bugs and the fight and timeout problems.\n\n**What was the least helpful test you ran?**\nThe determinism hash test: it passed the first time and never caught anything.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n**What did you like most about the engine?**\nOne height rule shared by collision, sight, reach and navigation: a TileMap with heights, E.Mover's parkour, E.sees, E.Suspicion and FlowField gave a working stealth sandbox almost at once, and exact fixed-step headless play (game.advance) made scripted playthroughs and a mock hub easy.\n\n**Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\nYes, a few times: a queue item lifted by a footprint sorts over actors standing on that block; r.overlay draws over everything, so a painted room has to go straight to r.ctx; E.Suspicion never decays while the target is seen, so a faint exposure still builds up; the Humanoid's blink draws Math.random in update (it matters on the hub's card); CSS zoom does not scale percentage heights; a custom input map has to list the menu actions itself.\n\n**What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?**\nThe stealth layer: a baked light map and exposure (light x cover x motion x crouch), Shadow Sight and the Ki Gauge, a guard brain with bait, bodies, bells and reinforcements; and the mission runtime (objectives, triggers, checkpoints) that the campaign, the Workshop and the hub round share.\n\n**What was the hardest part about using the engine?**\nDepth-sorting big drawn roofs (kawara caps, hall roofs) against the actors in a height map of one column per cell, and making the HTML menus and the canvas HUD read at 10 feet.\n\n**What did you change in the engine, and why?**\nNine small patches, marked BENTOU PATCH in the engine and listed on the Credits page: font glyphs; PlayStation symbols by default with an Xbox option; Humanoid masks, hats, spear, bow, club, an offhand blade and a sashimono; settings rows on custom Shell screens and a Dev group kept off the player's Settings; hover moves the focus; the 10-foot UI scale; music pluck, attack and release envelopes; a voice bus; the hub's Create + Options guard.\n\n**If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?**\nA first-class roof or canopy primitive (or a queue option) that sorts per cell, so actors standing on a block draw over its cap. Big drawn overhangs are the main gap for towns and castles.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n**What did you like most about this prompt?**\nConcrete deliverables with an exact done condition, a deep plan to follow, the one-command test rule (failures only), and a real hub harness to check against.\n\n**What was confusing?**\nThe plan's file names carried another run's model and timestamp; the title rule (brainstorm 50 and draw with an RNG) next to a plan that had already drawn the title; and how to report usage when the agent cannot see its own token counts.\n\n**What was the hardest thing to do?**\nThe scope: four missions with bosses, a mission editor, hub multiplayer, attract mode and dev tools in one pass, judging the look only from headless screenshots.\n\n**What would you change in this prompt?**\nAdd a ranked must-have list (what to cut first if time runs short), give the plan this run's names, and say how to report usage when it is not visible."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1460,"cache_read_input_tokens":40182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1460},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58a16430-39e5-4d69-a4e7-fa8db44e4654","uuid":"505f20f2-5540-46f5-b269-9a8272632397","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:32:30.980Z","request_id":"req_011CghBYuZdea7FCFQ4WEQoK"}
