{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VSzNGj6mZhRSy51Ny9uvDM","type":"tool_result","content":"49:Design the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow t\n9222:const SHELL_GROUPS = ['Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort'];\n    b.onclick = () => { const v = this._set(key, !S[key]); b.textContent = v ? 'On' : 'Off'; b.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(!!v)); };\n    row.appendChild(b); return row;\n  }\n  /** the settings screen's rows: Display, Sound and Comfort, then the game's own (standard: false, the game's items only) */\n  _settingsRows(add) {\n    const S = this._game.settings, own = this._items().map(i => i.key);\n    if (!this._std) { for (const k of own) add(this._row(k)); return; }\n    const groups = SHELL_GROUPS.concat([...new Set(S.keys().map(k => S.spec(k).group))].filter(g => !SHELL_GROUPS.includes(g) && !['Controls', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Dev'].includes(g)));   // BENTOU PATCH 4: the Dev group's sliders live on the dev screens onl\n    for (const g of groups) {\n      const keys = S.keys(g).filter(k => (k !== 'scale' || this._game.screen._fixedRes()) && (k !== 'fullscreen' || this._game.o.fullscreen !== false) && (k !== 'zoom' || !this._game._zoomStd() || this._game._zooms()) && S.spec(k).type !== 'value');\n      if (!keys.length) continue;\n      add(this._el('div', 'esh-k esh-sec', g)); for (const k of keys) add(this._row(k));\n    }\n  }\n  /** the controls screen: each action's keys and buttons (press a new one to rebind), the controller's and the touch","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58a16430-39e5-4d69-a4e7-fa8db44e4654","uuid":"89526821-794e-47f2-86d4-67a2d273abe2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:35:38.811Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"49:Design the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow t\n9222:const SHELL_GROUPS = ['Display', 'Sound', 'Comfort'];\n    b.onclick = () => { const v = this._set(key, !S[key]); b.textContent = v ? 'On' : 'Off'; b.setAttribute('aria-checked', String(!!v)); };\n    row.appendChild(b); return row;\n  }\n  /** the settings screen's rows: Display, Sound and Comfort, then the game's own (standard: false, the game's items only) */\n  _settingsRows(add) {\n    const S = this._game.settings, own = this._items().map(i => i.key);\n    if (!this._std) { for (const k of own) add(this._row(k)); return; }\n    const groups = SHELL_GROUPS.concat([...new Set(S.keys().map(k => S.spec(k).group))].filter(g => !SHELL_GROUPS.includes(g) && !['Controls', 'Controller', 'Touch', 'Dev'].includes(g)));   // BENTOU PATCH 4: the Dev group's sliders live on the dev screens onl\n    for (const g of groups) {\n      const keys = S.keys(g).filter(k => (k !== 'scale' || this._game.screen._fixedRes()) && (k !== 'fullscreen' || this._game.o.fullscreen !== false) && (k !== 'zoom' || !this._game._zoomStd() || this._game._zooms()) && S.spec(k).type !== 'value');\n      if (!keys.length) continue;\n      add(this._el('div', 'esh-k esh-sec', g)); for (const k of keys) add(this._row(k));\n    }\n  }\n  /** the controls screen: each action's keys and buttons (press a new one to rebind), the