150, jitter 50, loss 5; the host leaving); screenshots only for the look\n- **Research:** The planner's research (the Wikipedia article on Tenchu 2; the engine's handoff docs; the AI Hub README and harness) plus the engine and hub docs read for this build; no web search during the build\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\n- **Usage:** API cost and tokens: unknown (not visible to the agent). Session time: about 2 hours 15 minutes (18:33 to about 20:50).\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n\n**How many issues did testing catch?**\n27. The scripted tests caught 18 (in the game, the autopilot, the level data and one in the engine's Settings screen) and screenshot reviews caught 9 visual and layout issues. Each is listed in tests/ISSUES.md with how it was found and fixed.\n\n**How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?**\n4: guards attacking Tobei while he was still caged (the alarm bell could fail Kiri Lake), the water-gate lever taken by Tobei's wait / follow toggle (it blocked the escort), sleeping guards woken by their own snores (it broke the Sleep Dango and a Trial step), and the roof caps drawing over people standing on a roof (Kurogane's fight on the keep top was hidden).\n\n**What was the most helpful test you ran?**\nThe scripted playthrough of the whole story (autopilot routes through all four missions, the ending, the credits, Kaede's run and the Night Delivery). It found both Tobei bugs and the fight and timeout problems.\n\n**What was the least helpful test you ran?**","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014DGGpgyhauJF63JmQYkaKV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
