{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B4wUSYQ4aF38pW13wP7Hxm","type":"tool_result","content":"## about\nsix About pages;every page has words;the feedback pages answer 4, 6 and 4 questions;the About screen pages through;exit-interview.json parses;it answers every Source Information field;its feedback matches the pages;its AI Hub entry is complete;\n\n## ai\na patrol walks its route;and back again;a post sweeps its gaze;a sleeper sleeps;a loud noise wakes it;a hound smells the hero and barks;an archer with a clear line looses arrows;no clear line (behind the storehouse): no arrows;a Red Lantern ninja climbs onto the roof;a civilian who sees the hero screams and flees;\n\n## alarm\nan alert samurai runs for the bell;the bell rings;reinforcements after the delay;killing the runner keeps the bell silent;an alert brings the alert layers;they fade out after it;\n\n## attract\nattract runs three loops;every vignette was visited each loop;no beat needed its timeout;any input returns to the title;\n\n## boot\nthe title after boot;no attract before 10 s;attract after 10 s idle;attract plays a vignette;a press returns to the title;\n\n## bosses\nthe monk kneels: \"Well struck.\";the court\\'s gate opens after Gonroku;\n\n## combat\nSojiro\\'s first slash deals 14 x 1.2;the block takes 85% (Sojiro);a parry inside the window staggers;the riposte kills a staggered ashigaru;a parry outside the window does not;i-frames: one hit of two lands;mid-roll, invulnerable;the block takes 70% (Kaede);death: the game-over overlay;retry restores the checkpoint;\n\n## determinism\nthe same input gives the same game;\n\n## dev\nevery dev page opens;god mode;invisible to guards;no-clip walks through walls;infinite tools;one-hit kills;freeze AI;reveal all enemies;a slider changes B.T live;the hero runs faster at once;Reset page (Hero) restores its sliders;Reset all restores every slider;dev settings stay off the player\\'s Settings;\n\n## grapple\nan anchor at the storehouse edge;a tap pulls the hero onto the roof;no anchor through a wall (the townhouse\\'s far side);the range slider limits the reach;the mouse picks the anchor under it;\n\n## hub\nconnect({ mode: ghost, seats: [1, 4], card: true });ready() with no key press;the game\\'s own card;no title, no attract;the card draws no Math.random numbers;Enter / cross answers Ready;triangle answers More time;start enters the round;nothing moves before time() reaches 0;progress from the first moment of play;sends at about 10 Hz, unreliable;progress about once a second;a ghost appears where the other player is;leave removes the ghost;no quit, no dev mode in a session;time-up: the result at once;only one result;end: no more input;end: sound off, nothing more sent;\n\n## input\nkeys: Space;the pad shows PlayStation symbols by default;the Xbox option shows A;a pad prompt: the pad code;a mouse prompt: the mouse button;a keyboard prompt: the key;the d-pad does not move the hero;the d-pad picks the next tool;the wheel cycles tools;the keys move the hero;\n\n## ki\nthe Ki number at 80 is 50;in plain view the guard is visible;behind the townhouse it is sensed;beyond the Ki range, and out of sight, it is hidden;Ki Focus senses further;\n\n## mission\nescape waits for the kill and the boss;the ledger is optional and active;taking the ledger completes the optional task;a trigger fires once;the kill completes its objective, the boss shows;escape opens after both;the moon timer fails the mission;the lord raises his cup (the fail cutscene);then the fail overlay in the mission;Tobei falls: the mission fails;the generic fail hook;a checkpoint restores objectives and the hero;the detection penalty is capped at three;the score formula;rank thresholds;unlocks by rank;the save round trip;\n\n## move\nruns at the run speed;a light tilt walks (50);crouched it sneaks (32);vaults the bamboo fence;climbs a 30 wall;cannot climb a 40 roof (it needs the grapple);deep water swims;crouch dives;diving is unseen (exposure 0);breath runs down underwater;out of breath, it drowns;crouch again surfaces;the shallows slow the run;crouched against a wall it hugs it;the hug slides along the wall, and peeks at its end;pushing away leaves the wall;a fall over 72 hurts;\n\n## perception\na lit hero 60 ahead is caught within 2 s;crouched in shadow at 100 stays calm;a hero on a roof right above is out of view;crouch-walking is not heard;running at 50 is heard;smoke blocks sight;crouched in tall grass, unseen;lightning exposes;a body is found: heightened;\n\n## playthrough\nevery story mission is completed in the save;the ending leads to the credits;the credits return to the title;Rice and Ash as Kaede is won;the Night Delivery is won;the trial shows its board;\n\n## silentcut\nbehind and close: Back;behind but too far: none;at its side, calm: Side;in front of an awake guard: none;in front of a sleeping guard: Front;never on an alert guard;on a roof over a guard: From above;from the water beside the bank: Undertow;never on a boss;a Silent Cut scores 150;\n\n## story\nevery briefing and debrief scene exists;scene ;lines of their own for Sojiro and Kaede;every spoken line exists;every bark category has lines;every rank has Granny\\'s word;\n\n## tools\nRice Ball: +40;Sour Plum: stamina and soft steps;Straw Cloak: 15 s;Poison Rice Ball: a guard eats it and dies;Sleep Dango: the eater sleeps;Shuriken: 8 damage;Shuriken: a calm guard turns to look;Smoke Bomb: a cloud at the feet;Smoke Bomb: the guard inside is blinded and loses the hero;Caltrops: damage, a stun and a limp;Firecracker: the guard goes to look where it popped;Fire Pot: 45 around it;giving fills compartments up to their stack;locked tools stay off the shelf;the suggested bento skips locked tools;\n\n## workshop\nthe editor builds a level;its objectives come from what is placed;a full level validates;a missing exit is caught;an unreachable target is caught;a slot keeps the level exactly;export and import round trip;import rejects what is not a level;a test play is won;\n\n## bundle\nthe head: charset, then the session client, then the hub tags;the hub goal and howto are short enough;the title after boot;a controller press switches the prompts to its symbols;a key press switches them back to keys;attract mode after 10 s without input;a mouse move returns to the title;a mission plays from the single file;no console errors;a touch-only device gets the controller-or-keyboard notice;attract still runs on a touch-only device;no errors on the phone;\n\n## hub\nthe served page is this game;the hub harness passes: ;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58a16430-39e5-4d69-a4e7-fa8db44e4654","uuid":"7d0934f4-0012-4b2c-a83d-597a920c003e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:44:19.137Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## about\nsix About pages;every page has words;the feedback pages answer 4, 6 and 4 questions;the About screen pages through;exit-interview.json parses;it answers every Source Information field;its feedback matches the pages;its AI Hub entry is complete;\n\n## ai\na patrol walks its route;and back again;a post sweeps its gaze;a sleeper sleeps;a loud noise wakes it;a hound smells the hero and barks;an archer with a clear line looses arrows;no clear line (behind the storehouse): no arrows;a Red Lantern ninja climbs onto the roof;a civilian who sees the hero screams and flees;\n\n## alarm\nan alert samurai runs for the bell;the bell rings;reinforcements after the delay;killing the runner keeps the bell silent;an alert brings the alert layers;they fade out after it;\n\n## attract\nattract runs three loops;every vignette was visited each loop;no beat needed its timeout;any input returns to the title;\n\n## boot\nthe title after boot;no attract before 10 s;attract after 10 s idle;attract plays a vignette;a press returns to the title;\n\n## bosses\nthe monk kneels: \"Well struck.\";the court\\'s gate opens after Gonroku;\n\n## combat\nSojiro\\'s first slash deals 14 x 1.2;the block takes 85% (Sojiro);a parry inside the window staggers;the riposte kills a staggered ashigaru;a parry outside the window does not;i-frames: one hit of two lands;mid-roll, invulnerable;the block takes 70% (Kaede);death: the game-over overlay;retry restores the checkpoint;\n\n## determinism\nthe same input gives the same game;\n\n## dev\nevery dev page opens;god mode;invisible to guards;no-clip walks through walls;infinite tools;one-hit kills;freeze AI;reveal all enemies;a slider changes B.T live;the hero runs faster at once;Reset page (Hero) restores its sliders;Reset all restores every slider;dev settings stay off the player\\'s Settings;\n\n## grapple\nan anchor at the storehouse edge;a tap pulls the hero onto the roof;no anchor through a wall (the townhouse\\'s far side);the range slider limits the reach;the mouse picks the anchor under it;\n\n## hub\nconnect({ mode: ghost, seats: [1, 4], card: true });ready() with no key press;the game\\'s own card;no title, no attract;the card draws no Math.random numbers;Enter / cross answers Ready;triangle answers More time;start enters the round;nothing moves before time() reaches 0;progress from the first moment of play;sends at about 10 Hz, unreliable;progress about once a second;a ghost appears where the other player is;leave removes the ghost;no quit, no dev mode in a session;time-up: the result at once;only one result;end: no more input;end: sound off, nothing more sent;\n\n## input\nkeys: Space;the pad shows PlayStation symbols by default;the Xbox option shows A;a pad prompt: the pad code;a mouse prompt: the mouse button;a keyboard prompt: the key;the d-pad does not move the hero;the d-pad picks the next tool;the wheel cycles tools;the keys move the hero;\n\n## ki\nthe Ki number at 80 is 50;in plain view the guard is visible;behind the townhouse it is sensed;beyond the Ki range, and out of sight, it is hidden;Ki Focus senses further;\n\n## mission\nescape waits for the kill and the boss;the ledger is optional and active;taking the ledger completes the optional task;a trigger fires once;the kill completes its objective, the boss shows;escape opens after both;the moon timer fails the mission;the lord raises his cup (the fail cutscene);then the fail overlay in the mission;Tobei falls: the mission fails;the generic fail hook;a checkpoint restores objectives and the hero;the detection penalty is capped at three;the score formula;rank thresholds;unlocks by rank;the save round trip;\n\n## move\nruns at the run speed;a light tilt walks (50);crouched it sneaks (32);vaults the bamboo fence;climbs a 30 wall;cannot climb a 40 roof (it needs the grapple);deep water swims;crouch dives;diving is unseen (exposure 0);breath runs down underwater;out of breath, it drowns;crouch again surfaces;the shallows slow the run;crouched against a wall it hugs it;the hug slides along the wall, and peeks at its end;pushing away leaves the wall;a fall over 72 hurts;\n\n## perception\na lit hero 60 ahead is caught within 2 s;crouched in shadow at 100 stays calm;a hero on a roof right above is out of view;crouch-walking is not heard;running at 50 is heard;smoke blocks sight;crouched in tall grass, unseen;lightning exposes;a body is found: heightened;\n\n## playthrough\nevery story mission is completed in the save;the ending leads to the credits;the credits return to the title;Rice and Ash as Kaede is won;the Night Delivery is won;the trial shows its board;\n\n## silentcut\nbehind and close: Back;behind but too far: none;at its side, calm: Side;in front of an awake guard: none;in front of a sleeping guard: Front;never on an alert guard;on a roof over a guard: From above;from the water beside the bank: Undertow;never on a boss;a Silent Cut scores 150;\n\n## story\nevery briefing and debrief scene exists;scene ;lines of their own for Sojiro and Kaede;every spoken line exists;every bark category has lines;every rank has Granny\\'s word;\n\n## tools\nRice Ball: +40;Sour Plum: stamina and soft steps;Straw Cloak: 15 s;Poison Rice Ball: a guard eats it and dies;Sleep Dango: the eater sleeps;Shuriken: 8 damage;Shuriken: a calm guard turns to look;Smoke Bomb: a cloud at the feet;Smoke Bomb: the guard inside is blinded and loses the hero;Caltrops: damage, a stun and a limp;Firecracker: the guard goes to look where it popped;Fire Pot: 45 around it;giving fills compartments up to their stack;locked tools stay off the shelf;the suggested bento skips locked tools;\n\n## workshop\nthe editor builds a level;its objectives come from what is placed;a full level validates;a missing exit is caught;an unreachable target is caught;a slot keeps the level exactly;export and import round trip;import rejects what is not a level;a test play is won;\n\n## bundle\nthe head: charset, then the session client, then the hub tags;the hub goal and howto are short enough;the title after boot;a controller press switches the prompts to its symbols;a key press switches them back to keys;attract mode after 10 s without input;a mouse move returns to the title;a mission plays from the single file;no console errors;a touch-only device gets the controller-or-keyboard notice;attract still runs on a touch-only device;no errors on the phone;\n\n## hub\nthe served page is this game;the hub harness passes: ;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B4wUSYQ4aF38pW13wP7Hxm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
