{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and parse, and the final reply has all four sections. But the transcript shows the test run 'passing' does not establish TASK.md feature completeness. The main gap is the Testing Feedback claim 'the determinism hash test ... never caught anything' and the 'most helpful test' claim were not grounded in a verified count (the transcript grep found 0 determinism FAIL lines, but the determinism suite itself is one check, so it is only weakly supported). More importantly, the audit (tools/audit.mjs) passes items on the basis of regex patterns chosen by the agent and asserts several requirements through shallow checks, e.g. 'Genre' is supported by ninety unrelated checks and 'Art' only by one drawn-prop check, so 'every feature implemented' is not demonstrated by independent evidence. Also, the file-name decision (Bentou2 instead of the TASK.md GameTitle form) was reasoned from the plan rather than from TASK.md's own rule, which is a deviation the hook can reasonably flag."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58a16430-39e5-4d69-a4e7-fa8db44e4654","uuid":"6933c97d-7adb-4e18-b08a-f4e8212fe4b8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:59:13.752Z","isSynthetic":true}
