{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghGf6qnU8EgX25WnhMiM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The feedback repeats last round's points almost word for word, so I'll answer the two concrete ones and be plain about the third:\n- **Art, \"one drawn-prop check plus screenshots\".** The engine author's checker had only been run by hand. I'll make it part of the test command on every mission, asserting no errors, no look notes, and colour and fill above set levels. That puts a verdict from a tool I didn't write into the Art item.\n- **Genre, \"broad suites\".** I'll turn the stealth measurements from the real Rice and Ash level into checks, so the Genre item has its own specific ones.\n- **\"No independent verification\".** TASK.md line 28 forbids using subagents to review, judge or audit, so I won't add an agent auditor. A human review of the evidence is the remaining step."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5573,"cache_read_input_tokens":360997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5573},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58a16430-39e5-4d69-a4e7-fa8db44e4654","uuid":"adfb2abf-a6c4-4546-9ead-97b7655926f1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:39:28.326Z","request_id":"req_011CghGf6VTWZD8ZLbVy4Ci8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghGf6qnU8EgX25WnhMiM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FKQDe7puNiDT5FPQjTp3or","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > tests/stealth.test.mjs <<'EOF'\n// stealth: the stealth model in a real level (Rice and Ash), at the guard whose view has the most light contrast: standing\n// in its lantern light gets you caught, crouching in its shadow does not; creeping behind it is silent, running is heard;\n// an alerted samurai runs for the alarm bell\nexport default async function (t) {\n  const { B, check, game } = t; t.step(.3);\n  t.load('m1', { mode: 'story', character: 'sojiro' }); B.Cutscene.clear(); t.step(.5);\n  const M = B.M, h = M.hero, W = M.world;\n  const spots = g => { const cf = Math.cos(g.facing), sf = Math.sin(g.facing), at = (d, lat) => ({ x: g.x + cf * d - sf * lat, y: g.y + sf * d + cf * lat, d });\n    const flat = p => [0, 8, 16, 24].every(k => Math.abs(W.map.groundAt(p.x - sf * k, p.y + cf * k) - g.z) < 1) && Math.abs(W.map.groundAt(p.x, p.y) - g.z) < 1;\n    const pick = (d0, d1, better) => { let best = null; for (let d = d0; d <= d1; d += 6) for (const lat of [-18, -9, 0, 9, 18]) { const p = at(d, lat); if (!flat(p)) continue; p.l = W.lightAt(p.x, p.y, g.z); if (!best || better(p.l, best.l)) best = p; } return best; };\n    const lit = pick(50, 70, (a, b) => a > b), dark = pick(80, 120, (a, b) => a < b); let back = null;\n    for (const lat of [0, -10, 10, -20, 20]) { const p = at(-30, lat); p.z = g.z; if (flat(p) && W.map.ray(g, p, { eye: 20, target: 4 }).clear) { back = p; break; } }\n    return lit && dark && back ? { lit, dark, back, side: [-sf, cf], score: lit.l - dark.l } : null; };\n  const cand = M.guards.filter(x => x.alive && !x.asleep && x.mind && (x.type === 'ashigaru' || x.type === 'samurai')).map(x => [x, spots(x)]).filter(c => c[1]).sort((a, b) => b[1].score - a[1].score);\n  if (!check('a guard with lantern light and shadow in its view, and open ground behind it', cand.length > 0, '')) return;\n  const [g, S] = cand[0]; g.mode = 'stand'; const gx = g.x, gy = g.y, gf = g.facing;\n  const steps = []; B.on('noise', e => { if (e.kind === 'step') steps.push(e.loud); });\n  const trial = (p, crouch, secs, move) => { g.mind.reset(); g.target = null; Object.assign(g, { x: gx, y: gy, facing: gf }); steps.length = 0;\n    game.debug.teleport(p.x, p.y, W.map.groundAt(p.x, p.y), gf + Math.PI); h.crouch = crouch; let tA = null, peak = 0;\n    for (let k = 0; k < secs * 20; k++) { B.testIntent = move ? { move } : {}; game.advance(.05); B.testIntent = null; h.crouch = crouch; peak = Math.max(peak, g.mind.level); if (tA === null && g.mind.state === 'alert') tA = (k + 1) * .05; }\n    return { tA, peak, state: g.mind.state, steps: steps.length }; };\n  let r = trial(S.lit, false, 3); check('standing in a guard\\'s lantern light 50 px ahead: alerted within 3 s', r.tA !== null && S.lit.l > S.dark.l + .15, JSON.stringify(r) + ' light ' + S.lit.l.toFixed(2));\n  r = trial(S.dark, true, 5); check('crouched in its shadow 80-120 px ahead: never suspicious in 5 s', r.peak < .2 && r.state === 'calm', JSON.stringify(r) + ' light ' + S.dark.l.toFixed(2));\n  r = trial(S.back, true, 1, S.side); check('creeping 30 px behind it: no step noise, it stays calm', r.steps === 0 && r.state === 'calm', JSON.stringify(r));\n  r = trial(S.back, false, .7, S.side); check('running 30 px behind it: its steps are heard', r.steps > 0 && r.peak > .5, JSON.stringify(r));\n  g.mind.reset(); const home = M.level.hero.at, hx = (home[0] + .5) * 16, hy = (home[1] + .5) * 16; game.debug.teleport(hx, hy, W.map.groundAt(hx, hy));\n  let bell = 0; B.on('bell', () => bell++); const sam = M.guards.find(x => x.alive && x.type === 'samurai'); game.debug.alert(sam.id); t.step(14);\n  check('an alerted samurai rings the alarm bell within 14 s', bell > 0, sam.id);\n}\nEOF\ncat > tests/browser/enginecheck.mjs <<'EOF'\n// browser/enginecheck: the engine author's own checker (handoff/tools/check.mjs, not written for this game) on the shipped\n// file, every mission: it plays each for a moment in Chromium, turns through the views, and judges the look against its\n// PS1-era bar (distinct colours, flat area, contrast). Each mission must show no errors and draw no look notes\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { rmSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { NAME } from '../../tools/name.mjs';\nexport default async function ({ dev, check }) {\n  const file = join(dev, '..', NAME + '.html');\n  for (const id of ['training', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3']) {\n    const out = join(dev, '.enginecheck-' + id);\n    const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, [join(dev, 'handoff', 'tools', 'check.mjs'), file + '#' + id, '--out', out], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 150000 });\n    const txt = (r.stdout || '') + (r.stderr || ''), play = txt.split('\\n').find(l => /after play\\s+scene mission/.test(l)) || '';\n    const colors = +((play.match(/(\\d+) colors/) || [])[1] || 0), filled = +((play.match(/(\\d+)% filled/) || [])[1] || 0);\n    check(`the engine's checker on ${id}: no errors`, r.status === 0 && /\\bno errors\\b/.test(txt), txt.split('\\n').filter(l => /error/i.test(l)).slice(0, 3).join(' | ') || 'exit ' + r.status);\n    check(`the engine's checker on ${id}: no look notes against its PS1-era bar (${colors} colours, ${filled}% filled)`, !/look notes/.test(txt) && colors >= 60 && filled >= 80, play.trim());\n    rmSync(out, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode tests/run.mjs --fast stealth 2>&1 | tail -4; node tests/run.mjs --browser enginecheck 2>&1 | tail -4","description":"Add stealth and engine-checker suites; run both","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5573,"cache_read_input_tokens":360997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5573},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58a16430-39e5-4d69-a4e7-fa8db44e4654","uuid":"895740d3-a1fd-4104-b6e7-f19751b550c4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T04:39:48.695Z","request_id":"req_011CghGf6VTWZD8ZLbVy4Ci8","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01FKQDe7puNiDT5FPQjTp3or":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183331__xf7f297/work/Bentou2BirthOfTheLunchboxAssassins-Tenchu2BirthOfTheStealthAssassins-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331 && cat > tests/stealth.test.mjs <<'EOF'\n// stealth: the stealth model in a real level (Rice and Ash), at the guard whose view has the most light contrast: standing\n// in its lantern light gets you caught, crouching in its shadow does not; creeping behind it is silent, running is heard;\n// an alerted samurai runs for the alarm bell\nexport default async function (t) {\n  const { B, check, game } = t; t.step(.3);\n  t.load('m1', { mode: 'story', character: 'sojiro' }); B.Cutscene.clear(); t.step(.5);\n  const M = B.M, h = M.hero, W = M.world;\n  const spots = g => { const cf = Math.cos(g.facing), sf = Math.sin(g.facing), at = (d, lat) => ({ x: g.x + cf * d - sf * lat, y: g.y + sf * d + cf * lat, d });\n    const flat = p => [0, 8, 16, 24].every(k => Math.abs(W.map.groundAt(p.x - sf * k, p.y + cf * k) - g.z) < 1) && Math.abs(W.map.groundAt(p.x, p.y) - g.z) < 1;\n    const pick = (d0, d1, better) => { let best = null; for (let d = d0; d <= d1; d += 6) for (const lat of [-18, -9, 0, 9, 18]) { const p = at(d, lat); if (!flat(p)) continue; p.l = W.lightAt(p.x, p.y, g.z); if (!best || better(p.l, best.l)) best = p; } return best; };\n    const lit = pick(50, 70, (a, b) => a > b), dark = pick(80, 120, (a, b) => a < b); let back = null;\n    for (const lat of [0, -10, 10, -20, 20]) { const p = at(-30, lat); p.z = g.z; if (flat(p) && W.map.ray(g, p, { eye: 20, target: 4 }).clear) { back = p; break; } }\n    return lit && dark && back ? { lit, dark, back, side: [-sf, cf], score: lit.l - dark.l } : null; };\n  const cand = M.guards.filter(x => x.alive && !x.asleep && x.mind && (x.type === 'ashigaru' || x.type === 'samurai')).map(x => [x, spots(x)]).filter(c => c[1]).sort((a, b) => b[1].score - a[1].score);\n  if (!check('a guard with lantern light and shadow in its view, and open ground behind it', cand.length > 0, '')) return;\n  const [g, S] = cand[0]; g.mode = 'stand'; const gx = g.x, gy = g.y, gf = g.facing;\n  const steps = []; B.on('noise', e => { if (e.kind === 'step') steps.push(e.loud); });\n  const trial = (p, crouch, secs, move) => { g.mind.reset(); g.target = null; Object.assign(g, { x: gx, y: gy, facing: gf }); steps.length = 0;\n    game.debug.teleport(p.x, p.y, W.map.groundAt(p.x, p.y), gf + Math.PI); h.crouch = crouch; let tA = null, peak = 0;\n    for (let k = 0; k < secs * 20; k++) { B.testIntent = move ? { move } : {}; game.advance(.05); B.testIntent = null; h.crouch = crouch; peak = Math.max(peak, g.mind.level); if (tA === null && g.mind.state === 'alert') tA = (k + 1) * .05; }\n    return { tA, peak, state: g.mind.state, steps: steps.length }; };\n  let r = trial(S.lit, false, 3); check('standing in a guard\\'s lantern light 50 px ahead: alerted within 3 s', r.tA !== null && S.lit.l > S.dark.l + .15, JSON.stringify(r) + ' light ' + S.lit.l.toFixed(2));\n  r = trial(S.dark, true, 5); check('crouched in its shadow 80-120 px ahead: never suspicious in 5 s', r.peak < .2 && r.state === 'calm', JSON.stringify(r) + ' light ' + S.dark.l.toFixed(2));\n  r = trial(S.back, true, 1, S.side); check('creeping 30 px behind it: no step noise, it stays calm', r.steps === 0 && r.state === 'calm', JSON.stringify(r));\n  r = trial(S.back, false, .7, S.side); check('running 30 px behind it: its steps are heard', r.steps > 0 && r.peak > .5, JSON.stringify(r));\n  g.mind.reset(); const home = M.level.hero.at, hx = (home[0] + .5) * 16, hy = (home[1] + .5) * 16; game.debug.teleport(hx, hy, W.map.groundAt(hx, hy));\n  let bell = 0; B.on('bell', () => bell++); const sam = M.guards.find(x => x.alive && x.type === 'samurai'); game.debug.alert(sam.id); t.step(14);\n  check('an alerted samurai rings the alarm bell within 14 s', bell > 0, sam.id);\n}\nEOF\ncat > tests/browser/enginecheck.mjs <<'EOF'\n// browser/enginecheck: the engine author's own checker (handoff/tools/check.mjs, not written for this game) on the shipped\n// file, every mission: it plays each for a moment in Chromium, turns through the views, and judges the look against its\n// PS1-era bar (distinct colours, flat area, contrast). Each mission must show no errors and draw no look notes\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { rmSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { NAME } from '../../tools/name.mjs';\nexport default async function ({ dev, check }) {\n  const file = join(dev, '..', NAME + '.html');\n  for (const id of ['training', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3']) {\n    const out = join(dev, '.enginecheck-' + id);\n    const r = spawnSync(process.execPath, [join(dev, 'handoff', 'tools', 'check.mjs'), file + '#' + id, '--out', out], { encoding: 'utf8', timeout: 150000 });\n    const txt = (r.stdout || '') + (r.stderr || ''), play = txt.split('\\n').find(l => /after play\\s+scene mission/.test(l)) || '';\n    const colors = +((play.match(/(\\d+) colors/) || [])[1] || 0), filled = +((play.match(/(\\d+)% filled/) || [])[1] || 0);\n    check(`the engine's checker on ${id}: no errors`, r.status === 0 && /\\bno errors\\b/.test(txt), txt.split('\\n').filter(l => /error/i.test(l)).slice(0, 3).join(' | ') || 'exit ' + r.status);\n    check(`the engine's checker on ${id}: no look notes against its PS1-era bar (${colors} colours, ${filled}% filled)`, !/look notes/.test(txt) && colors >= 60 && filled >= 80, play.trim());\n    rmSync(out, { recursive: true, force: true });\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode tests/run.mjs --fast stealth 2>&1 | tail -4; node tests/run.mjs --browser enginecheck 2>&1 | tail -4","description":"Add stealth and engine-checker suites; run both","timeout":400000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01FKQDe7puNiDT5FPQjTp3or":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-183331__xf7f297/work/Bentou2BirthOfTheLunchboxAssassins-Tenchu2BirthOfTheStealthAssassins-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-183331"}}}
